/-! ## 189. A canonical regular fixed point downstairs

The full normalized seam has a regular fixed centre.  Its orbit class is fixed by the intrinsic
quotient reflection, and the canonical regular homeomorphism carries it to a fixed point of the
actual reduced `edgeSigma`.  This supplies the final geometric datum required by the fixed-mirror
bridge without any moved-point or nontriviality assumption.
