      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 h

/-- **Advance 10.** The actual reduced unfolding now acquires a compact-polygon-compatible regular
translation surface whose construction contains no historical whole-half-plane edge cover. -/
noncomputable def boundedReducedSurface
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite) :
    RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface
      (X := _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D) := by
  let Sfull := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let hreg := boundedPreservesRegular
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let htrans := boundedLocalTranslationOnRegular
    (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  exact FullReducedCanonicalRegularSurfaceEffective.reducedSurface
    (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D Sfull hreg htrans

end BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation


/-! ## 268. Updated boundary after migrating redundancy to the bounded atlas

The compact-polygon repair now extends through the quotient surface itself.  Redundancy on a bounded
edge chart is handled directly by a finite coordinate-difference argument: no transported
whole-half-plane chart and no distinguished global boundary parameter is used.  Interior points use
the unchanged exact developing formula.  Consequently the repaired bounded full atlas carries the
actual redundancy subgroup by local translations, and the effective finite-orbit construction gives
a regular translation surface on the genuine reduced unfolding with no historical `FlatEdgeCover`
parameter anywhere in its type.

The next step is to reattach Sections 207--260 to this repaired `boundedReducedSurface`: the
intrinsic regular set is unchanged, so the finite/nonzero measure and quotient-measure results can be
reused; the only remaining assembly is to identify the repaired reduced local charts with the
interior/bounded-edge local measure laws and invoke the already-proved local-to-global
`ScalesFlatArea` criterion.  After that, the determinant-one branch is genuinely closed on the
non-vacuous compact-polygon surface.
-/

/-! ## 269. Reattaching concrete area to the repaired bounded surface

The repaired bounded atlas of Sections 261--268 allows an arbitrary copy label on every edge
window.  The packaged edge-area theorem of Section 243 was stated on the identity pair of copies.
Before descending area through the repaired quotient we therefore close that harmless but real
interface: the left `G`-action merely permutes the finitely many raw copies, hence preserves the
canonical raw and full measures.  The identity-copy edge density law can then be transported to an
arbitrary copy label.  We also package the finite/nonzero reduced regular measure on the repaired
bounded surface itself.
-/

