/-! ## 282. Updated boundary after closing normalized finite/nonzero mass

The orbit-degree normalization now has a complete global mass theory.  Its density is everywhere
positive and bounded by one; consequently normalization preserves nonzero mass and cannot destroy
finiteness.  After transport through the regular-orbit homeomorphism, this gives a finite nonzero
normalized measure directly on the repaired bounded reduced polygon surface.  Hence the
`IsFiniteNonzeroFlatArea` half of `HasFiniteFlatAreaScaling` is closed for the *same normalized
measure* whose refined quotient charts carry one-sheet density.

The remaining determinant-one task is now only `ScalesFlatArea`: combine Section 273's unit-density
physical full charts with Section 279's exact normalized one-sheet descent, identify the resulting
actual reduced chart coordinate measures with Lebesgue, and apply Section 259's local-to-global
scaling theorem to every affine automorphism.  No further finiteness, multiplicity, or normalization
argument is required.
-/

/-! ## 283. General real-affine change of variables directly on the complex plane

The repaired reduced charts are genuine translation charts in `ℂ`, while an affine automorphism
has an arbitrary invertible **real**-linear derivative `PlaneRealLinearEquiv`.  Sections 211--213
proved the general Jacobian theorem in `Fin 2 → ℝ`, and Sections 238--239 transported the special
complex-multiplication case back to `ℂ`.  For the final `ScalesFlatArea` assembly we must not
silently assume that an arbitrary affine derivative is complex-linear.  We therefore package the
full real-affine change-of-variables theorem directly on `ℂ`, including restrictions and an
arbitrary constant density.
-/

namespace GeneralComplexRealAffineJacobian

open MeasureTheory
open VeechAffineDerivative
open AffineFlatAreaScaling
open DevelopedPlaneLebesgueScaling
open FiniteDirectionalActionArea
open TranslationOverlapLebesgueConsistency

/-- **Advance 1.** The general complex-plane affine map with real-linear part `L`. -/
def planeAffineMap (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ) : ℂ → ℂ :=
  fun z => c + L z

/-- **Advance 2.** Every such affine map is measurable. -/
theorem measurable_planeAffineMap (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ) :
    Measurable (planeAffineMap L c) := by
  exact measurable_const.add (measurable_planeRealLinearEquiv L)

/-- **Advance 3.** The affine map is injective because its real-linear part is invertible. -/
theorem planeAffineMap_injective (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ) :
    Function.Injective (planeAffineMap L c) := by
  intro z w hzw
  have hlin : L z = L w := by
    exact add_left_cancel hzw
  have hinv := congrArg L.invFun hlin
  simpa using hinv

/-- **Advance 4.** Bundle the affine map as a measurable equivalence.  Its inverse is the literal
formula `w ↦ L⁻¹(w-c)`.  This provides measurable images without any appeal to a special complex
scalar normal form. -/
noncomputable def planeAffineMeasurableEquiv
    (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ) : ℂ ≃ᵐ ℂ where
  toEquiv :=
    { toFun := planeAffineMap L c
      invFun := fun w => (inv L) (w - c)
      left_inv := by
        intro z
        simp [planeAffineMap]
      right_inv := by
        intro w
        simp [planeAffineMap] }
  measurable_toFun := measurable_planeAffineMap L c
  measurable_invFun := by
    exact (measurable_planeRealLinearEquiv (inv L)).comp
      (measurable_id.sub measurable_const)

/-- **Advance 5.** The forward general real-affine map has exactly the reciprocal determinant
Jacobian. -/
theorem map_planeAffineMap_volume
    (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ) :
    Measure.map (planeAffineMap L c) (volume : Measure ℂ) =
      ENNReal.ofReal |(realDet L)⁻¹| • (volume : Measure ℂ) := by
  have hL : Measurable (fun z : ℂ => L z) :=
    measurable_planeRealLinearEquiv L
  have ht : Measurable (fun z : ℂ => c + z) :=
    measurable_const.add measurable_id
  change Measure.map ((fun z : ℂ => c + z) ∘ (fun z : ℂ => L z))
      (volume : Measure ℂ) = _
  rw [← Measure.map_map ht hL]
  rw [map_planeRealLinearEquiv_volume L]
  rw [Measure.map_smul
    (ENNReal.ofReal |(realDet L)⁻¹|) ht.aemeasurable]
  rw [map_complexTranslation_volume c]

/-- **Advance 6.** An arbitrary constant density commutes with the same affine Jacobian. -/
theorem map_planeAffineMap_smul_volume
    (k : ENNReal) (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ) :
    Measure.map (planeAffineMap L c) (k • (volume : Measure ℂ)) =
      ENNReal.ofReal |(realDet L)⁻¹| •
        (k • (volume : Measure ℂ)) := by
  rw [Measure.map_smul k
    (measurable_planeAffineMap L c).aemeasurable]
  rw [map_planeAffineMap_volume L c]
  simp [smul_smul, mul_comm]

/-- **Advance 7.** Specializing the affine linear part to `L⁻¹` gives exactly the project's
`jacobianScale L`, now directly on `ℂ`.  This is the local formula appearing in
`AffineAutomorphism.locally_affine_symm`. -/
theorem map_planeAffineMap_inv_volume
    (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ) :
    Measure.map (planeAffineMap (inv L) c) (volume : Measure ℂ) =
      jacobianScale L • (volume : Measure ℂ) := by
  rw [map_planeAffineMap_volume]
  rw [DevelopedPlaneLebesgueScaling.realDet_inv]
  simp [jacobianScale]

/-- **Advance 8.** Pushforward by a measurable equivalence commutes exactly with restriction to a
measurable source set.  This is the measurable-equivalence analogue of Section 259's homeomorphism
lemma and avoids any unnecessary continuity assumption in the measure calculation itself. -/
theorem map_restrict_measurableEquiv
    {A B : Type*} [MeasurableSpace A] [MeasurableSpace B]
    (e : A ≃ᵐ B) (μ : Measure A)
    {U : Set A} (hU : MeasurableSet U) :
    Measure.map e (μ.restrict U) =
      (Measure.map e μ).restrict (e '' U) := by
  apply Measure.ext
  intro V hV
  have hEU : MeasurableSet (e '' U) := e.measurableSet_image.mpr hU
  rw [Measure.map_apply e.measurable hV]
  rw [Measure.restrict_apply (hV.preimage e.measurable)]
  rw [Measure.restrict_apply hV]
  rw [Measure.map_apply e.measurable (hV.inter hEU)]
  congr 1
  ext x
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hxV, hxU⟩
    refine ⟨hxV, ?_⟩
    exact ⟨x, hxU, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨hxV, ⟨y, hyU, hyx⟩⟩
    have hxy : x = y := e.injective hyx.symm
    simpa [hxy] using And.intro hxV hyU

/-- **Advance 9.** Full restriction-level change of variables for a general real-affine map and an
arbitrary constant density. -/
theorem map_planeAffineMap_restrict_smul_volume
    (k : ENNReal) (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ)
    {U : Set ℂ} (hU : MeasurableSet U) :
    Measure.map (planeAffineMap L c)
        ((k • (volume : Measure ℂ)).restrict U) =
      (ENNReal.ofReal |(realDet L)⁻¹| •
        (k • (volume : Measure ℂ))).restrict
          (planeAffineMap L c '' U) := by
  have hrest := map_restrict_measurableEquiv
    (planeAffineMeasurableEquiv L c) (k • (volume : Measure ℂ)) hU
  have hmap := map_planeAffineMap_smul_volume k L c
  simpa [planeAffineMeasurableEquiv] using hrest.trans
    (congrArg (fun ν : Measure ℂ => ν.restrict
      (planeAffineMap L c '' U)) hmap)

/-- **Advance 10.** Exact local formula needed by `ScalesFlatArea`: an affine map whose derivative
is `L⁻¹` sends a constant-density Euclidean chart to the same density multiplied by
`jacobianScale L`, even after arbitrary Borel restriction.  No complex-linearity assumption on
`L` remains anywhere in the final affine-measure step. -/
theorem map_planeAffineMap_inv_restrict_smul_volume
    (k : ENNReal) (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ)
    {U : Set ℂ} (hU : MeasurableSet U) :
    Measure.map (planeAffineMap (inv L) c)
        ((k • (volume : Measure ℂ)).restrict U) =
      (jacobianScale L • (k • (volume : Measure ℂ))).restrict
        (planeAffineMap (inv L) c '' U) := by
  rw [map_planeAffineMap_restrict_smul_volume k (inv L) c hU]
  rw [DevelopedPlaneLebesgueScaling.realDet_inv]
  simp [jacobianScale]

end GeneralComplexRealAffineJacobian


/-! ## 284. Updated boundary after closing the general real-affine Jacobian gap

The final scaling argument no longer has any hidden complex-linearity restriction.  An arbitrary
`PlaneRealLinearEquiv` now has a direct affine realization on `ℂ`, with the exact reciprocal-
determinant pushforward formula, arbitrary constant densities, and Borel restrictions.  In
particular the local formula for derivative `L⁻¹` is literally `jacobianScale L`, exactly matching
`AffineAutomorphism.locally_affine_symm` and the definition of `ScalesFlatArea`.

Thus the remaining determinant-one work is now purely atlas/quotient assembly: combine the repaired
unit-density full charts with the normalized one-sheet reduced descent, transfer unit density to a
compatible reduced chart at every regular point, intersect those charts with the local affine
witness supplied by an arbitrary affine automorphism, apply Section 283's Advance 10, and invoke
Section 259's countable-local-restriction criterion.  There is no remaining Jacobian, finiteness,
normalization, or complex-linearity issue in that branch.
-/

/-! ## 285. Pointwise-local scaling and the second-countable global assembly

Section 259 globalized local restriction equalities after a *countable* covering family had already
been supplied.  An affine automorphism, however, naturally gives only one suitable neighbourhood at
each point.  The missing bridge is topological rather than measure-theoretic: on a second-countable
space, Mathlib's `countable_cover_nhds` extracts a countable subcover from any pointwise choice of
neighbourhoods.  We package this once and for all.  We also record that the finite orbit quotient of
a second-countable regular locus is again second-countable, and that the canonical homeomorphic
transport to the actual reduced regular locus preserves this property. -/

namespace PointwiseLocalScalingAssembly

open MeasureTheory
open TranslationAtlasGeometry
open TranslationAffineAutomorphisms
open VeechAffineDerivative
open AffineFlatAreaScaling
open ReducedLocalScalingAssembly
open ReducedQuotientTopology
open RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry
open RegularFiniteOrbitQuotient
open RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification

universe uX uH uY

/-- **Advance 1.** Two measures are locally restriction-equal if every point has an open
neighbourhood on which their restrictions literally coincide. -/
def LocallyRestrictionEqual
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    (μ ν : Measure X) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, ∃ U : Set X, IsOpen U ∧ x ∈ U ∧ μ.restrict U = ν.restrict U

/-- **Advance 2.** Choose one witnessing local equality neighbourhood at every point. -/
noncomputable def localEqualitySet
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    {μ ν : Measure X} (h : LocallyRestrictionEqual μ ν) (x : X) : Set X :=
  Classical.choose (h x)

/-- **Advance 3.** The chosen witness is open and contains its centre. -/
theorem localEqualitySet_open_mem
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    {μ ν : Measure X} (h : LocallyRestrictionEqual μ ν) (x : X) :
    IsOpen (localEqualitySet h x) ∧ x ∈ localEqualitySet h x := by
  exact ⟨(Classical.choose_spec (h x)).1,
    (Classical.choose_spec (h x)).2.1⟩

/-- **Advance 4.** The selected neighbourhood carries the promised restriction equality. -/
theorem restrict_localEqualitySet
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    {μ ν : Measure X} (h : LocallyRestrictionEqual μ ν) (x : X) :
    μ.restrict (localEqualitySet h x) = ν.restrict (localEqualitySet h x) := by
  exact (Classical.choose_spec (h x)).2.2

/-- **Advance 5.** In a second-countable space, the pointwise selected equality neighbourhoods
have a countable subcover. -/
theorem exists_countable_localEqualitySet_cover
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    [SecondCountableTopology X]
    {μ ν : Measure X} (h : LocallyRestrictionEqual μ ν) :
    ∃ s : Set X, s.Countable ∧
      ⋃ x ∈ s, localEqualitySet h x = Set.univ := by
  have hnhds : ∀ x : X, localEqualitySet h x ∈ nhds x := by
    intro x
    exact (localEqualitySet_open_mem h x).1.mem_nhds
      (localEqualitySet_open_mem h x).2
  exact TopologicalSpace.countable_cover_nhds hnhds

/-- **Advance 6.** Therefore pointwise local restriction equality implies global equality of
measures on a second-countable space.  No preselected countable atlas is needed. -/
theorem measure_eq_of_pointwise_local_restrictions
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    [SecondCountableTopology X]
    {μ ν : Measure X} (h : LocallyRestrictionEqual μ ν) :
    μ = ν := by
  rcases exists_countable_localEqualitySet_cover h with ⟨s, hs, hcover⟩
  exact Measure.ext_of_biUnion_eq_univ hs hcover
    (fun x _hx => restrict_localEqualitySet h x)

/-- **Advance 7.** The pointwise-local formulation of the flat-area scaling law.  It is exactly the
form naturally produced by intersecting an affine-normal-form witness with one normalized reduced
translation chart. -/
def PointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := X))
    [MeasurableSpace S.Regular] [BorelSpace S.Regular]
    (μ : Measure S.Regular) : Prop :=
  ∀ F : AffineAutomorphism S,
    LocallyRestrictionEqual
      (Measure.map (fun x => F.toHomeomorph.symm x) μ)
      (jacobianScale F.derivative • μ)

/-- **Advance 8.** On a second-countable regular locus, pointwise-local Jacobian scaling already
implies the global `ScalesFlatArea` property.  This removes the explicit countable-cover argument
from the final polygon theorem. -/
theorem scalesFlatArea_of_pointwise_local
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := X))
    [MeasurableSpace S.Regular] [BorelSpace S.Regular]
    [SecondCountableTopology S.Regular]
    (μ : Measure S.Regular)
    (hlocal : PointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea S μ) :
    ScalesFlatArea S μ := by
  intro F
  exact measure_eq_of_pointwise_local_restrictions (hlocal F)

/-- **Advance 9.** A finite locally translational orbit quotient of a second-countable regular
locus is second-countable.  This is precisely the quotient topology used by the effective reduced
atlas. -/
theorem regularOrbitQ_secondCountable
    {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
    [Group H] [Finite H]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y]
    [MulAction H Y] [ContinuousConstSMul H Y]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
    (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S) :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ [SecondCountableTopology S.Regular],
    SecondCountableTopology (_root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg) := by
  try dsimp only
  intro _inst0

  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular :=
    RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  have hquot : Topology.IsQuotientMap
      (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)) :=
    quotientMap_isQuotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
  have hopen : IsOpenMap (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)) :=
    quotientMap_isOpenMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
  exact Topology.IsOpenQuotientMap.secondCountableTopology
    ⟨hquot.surjective, hquot.continuous, hopen⟩

/-- **Advance 10.** The canonical actual reduced regular locus inherits second countability through
the regular-orbit homeomorphism.  Thus once the concrete full regular locus is shown
second-countable, the final normalized reduced measure can use Advance 8 with no further countable
atlas bookkeeping. -/
theorem canonicalReducedRegular_secondCountable
    {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
    [Group H] [Finite H]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y]
    [MulAction H Y] [ContinuousConstSMul H Y]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
    (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S) :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ [SecondCountableTopology S.Regular],
    SecondCountableTopology
      {z : ReducedQuotient.Q (H := H) (Y := Y) //
        z ∈ RegularFiniteOrbitQuotient.quotientRegular (H := H) S} := by
  try dsimp only
  intro _inst0

  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular :=
    RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  let : SecondCountableTopology (_root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg) :=
    PointwiseLocalScalingAssembly.regularOrbitQ_secondCountable (H := H) S hreg
  let e := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg
  exact e.symm.isEmbedding.secondCountableTopology

end PointwiseLocalScalingAssembly


/-! ## 286. Updated boundary after closing the pointwise-to-countable globalization gap

The final `ScalesFlatArea` assembly no longer needs a countable family of local scaling
neighbourhoods to be constructed by hand.  On any second-countable regular locus, one local
restriction equality at every point automatically admits a countable subcover, and therefore
implies the global measure equality.  Finite locally translational quotienting preserves second
countability, and the canonical homeomorphism to the actual reduced regular locus preserves it as
well.

Hence the remaining concrete task has sharpened to two local/topological statements: prove the
repaired full regular locus is second-countable (equivalently, establish this directly from its
finite-polygon quotient origin), and prove the normalized reduced area satisfies the pointwise local
restriction equality by combining Section 273's unit-density physical chart law, Section 280's
one-sheet normalized descent, and Section 284's general real-affine Jacobian formula.  Once those
are supplied, `scalesFlatArea_of_pointwise_local` closes the scaling law immediately.
-/

/-! ## 287. Second countability of the repaired bounded full/reduced surfaces

Section 285 reduced the global scaling problem to pointwise local restriction equalities plus
second countability of the repaired reduced regular locus.  We now prove that countability from the
actual finite-copy polygon origin, without imposing countability on the auxiliary interior/edge
chart index types.  The key point is that the raw finite-copy space is second-countable, hence
hereditarily Lindelöf; this property descends through the continuous surjective side-gluing map.
The repaired regular atlas is therefore a Lindelöf open-chart cover by chart sources homeomorphic to
open subsets of `ℂ`, so a countable subcover exists and yields second countability. -/

namespace RepairedSecondCountabilityClosure

open FullCopyUnfolding
open FullCopyUnfoldingTopology
open TranslationAtlasGeometry
open FullRegularFlatChartRestriction
open BoundedRegularAtlasRepair
open BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction
open BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation
open PointwiseLocalScalingAssembly
open RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry
open RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification
open ReducedQuotientTopology
open NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure
open AffineFlatAreaScaling

universe uG uE uI uJ

/-- **Advance 1.** The raw finite-copy polygon space is second-countable.  The finite discrete copy
label is second-countable, the planar polygon subtype is second-countable, and products preserve the
property. -/
theorem rawCopy_secondCountable
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G] :
    SecondCountableTopology (RawCopy (G := G) P₀.carrier) := by
  infer_instance

/-- **Advance 2.** Consequently the raw copy space is hereditarily Lindelöf. -/
theorem rawCopy_hereditarilyLindelof
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G] :
    HereditarilyLindelofSpace (RawCopy (G := G) P₀.carrier) := by
  let : SecondCountableTopology (RawCopy (G := G) P₀.carrier) :=
    rawCopy_secondCountable (G := G) P₀
  infer_instance

/-- **Advance 3.** The actual side-glued full unfolding is hereditarily Lindelöf.  This uses only
continuity and surjectivity of the genuine quotient map: every open subset downstairs is the image
of its open preimage upstairs, and that preimage is Lindelöf because the raw space is hereditarily
Lindelöf. -/
theorem full_hereditarilyLindelof
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G] :
    HereditarilyLindelofSpace (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D) := by
  let : SecondCountableTopology (RawCopy (G := G) P₀.carrier) :=
    rawCopy_secondCountable (G := G) P₀
  let : HereditarilyLindelofSpace (RawCopy (G := G) P₀.carrier) := inferInstance
  refine HereditarilyLindelofSpace.of_forall_isOpen ?_
  intro s hs
  let q := _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfoldingTopology.fullQuotientMap (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D
  have hpre : IsLindelof (q ⁻¹' s) :=
    HereditarilyLindelofSpace.isLindelof (q ⁻¹' s)
  have himg : IsLindelof (q '' (q ⁻¹' s)) :=
    hpre.image (fullQuotientMap_continuous
      (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)
  have hsur : Function.Surjective q :=
    (fullQuotientMap_isQuotientMap
      (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D).surjective
  have heq : q '' (q ⁻¹' s) = s := by
    ext y
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
      exact hx
    · intro hy
      rcases hsur y with ⟨x, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨x, hy, rfl⟩
  rw [heq] at himg
  exact himg

/-- **Advance 4.** The intrinsic regular subtype of the repaired full surface is Lindelöf (indeed
hereditarily Lindelöf), with no countability assumption on the chosen chart index sets. -/
theorem boundedFullRegular_lindelof
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite) :
    LindelofSpace
      (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
        (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).Regular := by
  let : HereditarilyLindelofSpace (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D) :=
    full_hereditarilyLindelof (G := G) H P₀ D
  infer_instance

/-- **Advance 5.** Every repaired regular chart source is second-countable, because the partial
homeomorphism identifies it homeomorphically with an open subset of the complex plane. -/
theorem boundedRegularChart_source_secondCountable
    {G : Type uG} [Group G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J)) :
    SecondCountableTopology
      ↑((BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
        (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a).source) := by
  let χ := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a
  let : SecondCountableTopology ↑χ.target := inferInstance
  exact χ.toHomeomorphSourceTarget.secondCountableTopology

/-- **Advance 6.** The repaired regular chart sources form an open cover of the whole repaired
regular subtype. -/
theorem boundedRegularChart_sources_cover
    {G : Type uG} [Group G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0) :
    (⋃ a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J),
      (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
        (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a).source) = Set.univ := by
  apply Set.Subset.antisymm (Set.subset_univ _)
  intro x hx
  rcases (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularCover
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0).covers x with ⟨a, ha⟩
  exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨a, ha⟩

/-- **Advance 7.** Lindelöfness extracts a countable subcover from the possibly huge repaired chart
family.  We package it as an `ℕ`-indexed family, so no countability assumption on `I` or `J` is ever
introduced. -/
theorem exists_nat_boundedRegularChart_cover
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite) :
    ∃ f : ℕ → BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J),
      (⋃ n : ℕ,
        (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
          (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 (f n)).source) = Set.univ := by
  let Sfull := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let : LindelofSpace Sfull.Regular :=
    boundedFullRegular_lindelof (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let : Nonempty (BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J)) := by
    let x0 : Sfull.Regular := Classical.choice
      (FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.regular_nonempty_of_atMostOne
        (G := G) (H := H) D g0 p0 hp0)
    rcases (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularCover
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0).covers x0 with ⟨a, ha⟩
    exact ⟨a⟩
  have hcoverEq := boundedRegularChart_sources_cover
    (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0
  have hcover : (Set.univ : Set Sfull.Regular) ⊆
      ⋃ a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J),
        (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
          (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a).source := by
    simpa [Sfull, hcoverEq]
  rcases (isLindelof_univ : IsLindelof (Set.univ : Set Sfull.Regular)).indexed_countable_subcover
        (fun a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J) =>
          (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
            (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a).source)
        (fun a => (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
          (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a).open_source)
        hcover with ⟨f, hf⟩
  refine ⟨f, Set.Subset.antisymm (Set.subset_univ _) ?_⟩
  exact hf

/-- **Advance 8.** The repaired full regular locus is second-countable, with no cardinality
hypothesis on the auxiliary cover indices. -/
theorem boundedFullRegular_secondCountable
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite) :
    SecondCountableTopology
      (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
        (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).Regular := by
  let Sfull := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  rcases exists_nat_boundedRegularChart_cover
      (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly with ⟨f, hf⟩
  let U : ℕ → Set Sfull.Regular := fun n =>
    (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 (f n)).source
  let : ∀ n : ℕ, SecondCountableTopology ↑(U n) := by
    intro n
    dsimp [U, Sfull]
    exact boundedRegularChart_source_secondCountable
      (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 (f n)
  exact TopologicalSpace.secondCountableTopology_of_countable_cover
    (U := U)
    (fun n => (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 (f n)).open_source)
    hf

/-- **Advance 9.** The actual repaired reduced regular locus is second-countable.  This is the
concrete specialization of Section 285's finite-orbit quotient theorem. -/
theorem boundedReducedRegular_secondCountable
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite) :
    SecondCountableTopology
      (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).Regular := by
  let Sfull := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let hreg := boundedPreservesRegular
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let : SecondCountableTopology Sfull.Regular :=
    boundedFullRegular_secondCountable
      (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  have hsc := canonicalReducedRegular_secondCountable (H := H) Sfull hreg
  dsimp only [BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface]
  convert! hsc using 1

/-- **Advance 10.** For the repaired bounded reduced surface, once the remaining pointwise local
Jacobian identity is proved, `ScalesFlatArea` follows immediately: second countability is no longer
an outstanding hypothesis. -/
theorem normalizedBoundedReducedArea_scales_of_pointwise
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (hlocal : PointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea
      (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
      (_root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)) :
    ScalesFlatArea
      (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
      (_root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly) := by
  let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let μred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let : SecondCountableTopology Sred.Regular :=
    boundedReducedRegular_secondCountable
      (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  exact scalesFlatArea_of_pointwise_local Sred μred hlocal

end RepairedSecondCountabilityClosure


/-! ## 288. Updated boundary after closing second countability on the repaired surface

The repaired compact-polygon surface now has its required countability topology intrinsically, with
no countability assumptions on the auxiliary chart index types.  The raw finite-copy polygon space
is second-countable and hereditarily Lindelöf; hereditary Lindelöfness descends through the actual
side-gluing quotient.  Hence the repaired regular chart cover has a countable subcover even when the
original cover indices are arbitrarily large.  Since every chart source is homeomorphic to an open
subset of `ℂ`, the repaired full regular locus is second-countable.  The finite locally translational
orbit quotient and canonical transport then make the repaired reduced regular locus second-countable
as well.

Consequently the determinant-one branch has now been reduced to exactly one substantive local
statement: `normalizedBoundedReducedArea` must satisfy `PointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea`.  Once this
pointwise statement is obtained by combining the repaired unit-density full charts, normalized
one-sheet descent, and the general real-affine restricted Jacobian formula, Advance 10 gives global
`ScalesFlatArea` immediately; Section 281 already supplies finite/nonzero total mass for the same
normalized measure.
-/

/-! ## 289. Repaired bounded charts cover the actual reduced regular locus compatibly

Section 288 reduced the determinant-one branch to a pointwise local measure statement.  Before
performing that measure calculation we remove the last chart-choice ambiguity.  Every point of the
actual repaired reduced regular locus is lifted canonically to one point of the intrinsic full
regular locus.  The repaired bounded atlas contains that lift in one of its genuine interior or
bounded-edge charts.  Section 160 then descends that concrete chart through an effective local
quotient sheet and transports it to the actual reduced regular locus.  The resulting chart contains
the original reduced point and is compatible with the preferred reduced atlas, hence differs from
the preferred chart locally by a translation only.

This is the exact topological interface needed by the remaining area argument: once unit Lebesgue
density is proved on the descended repaired chart, it transfers to the preferred reduced chart
without changing density, because the transition is a translation. -/

namespace RepairedReducedCompatibleChartCoverage

open TranslationAtlasGeometry
open TranslationAtlasCompatibleReplacement
open FullCopyUnfolding
open FullRegularFlatChartRestriction
open BoundedRegularAtlasRepair
open BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction
open BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation
open RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry
open RegularFiniteOrbitQuotient
open RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification
open ReducedQuotientTopology
open FreeTranslationQuotientAtlas
open QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart
open TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport
open CanonicalReducedCompatibleChartExistenceEffective
open CanonicalReducedRegularAtlasEffective

universe uH uY uG uE uI uJ

/-- **Advance 1.** Choose canonically one upstairs regular representative of every point of the
canonical reduced regular locus.  No freeness is used: the representative is chosen only after
passing to the intrinsic regular orbit quotient. -/
noncomputable def canonicalRegularLift
    {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
    [Group H] [MulAction H Y]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H Y] [Finite H]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
    (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S) :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (_x : {z : ReducedQuotient.Q (H := H) (Y := Y) //
      z ∈ quotientRegular (H := H) S}),
    S.Regular := by
  try dsimp only
  intro x

  letI : MulAction H S.Regular := regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  exact FreeTranslationQuotientAtlas.representative (H := H)
    ((regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg).symm x)

/-- **Advance 2.** The orbit of the chosen lift is exactly the intrinsic orbit corresponding to the
selected reduced regular point. -/
@[simp] theorem quotientMap_canonicalRegularLift
    {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
    [Group H] [MulAction H Y]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H Y] [Finite H]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
    (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S) :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (x : {z : ReducedQuotient.Q (H := H) (Y := Y) //
      z ∈ quotientRegular (H := H) S}),
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
        (canonicalRegularLift (H := H) S hreg x) =
      (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg).symm x := by
  try dsimp only
  intro x

  let : MulAction H S.Regular := regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  dsimp [canonicalRegularLift]
  exact FreeTranslationQuotientAtlas.quotientMap_representative
    (H := H) ((regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg).symm x)

/-- **Advance 3.** Transporting the orbit of the chosen lift back through the canonical
homeomorphism recovers the original reduced regular point literally. -/
@[simp] theorem canonicalRegularLift_maps_to
    {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
    [Group H] [MulAction H Y]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H Y] [Finite H]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
    (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S) :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (x : {z : ReducedQuotient.Q (H := H) (Y := Y) //
      z ∈ quotientRegular (H := H) S}),
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg)
        (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
          (canonicalRegularLift (H := H) S hreg x)) = x := by
  try dsimp only
  intro x

  rw [quotientMap_canonicalRegularLift (H := H) S hreg x]
  simp

/-- **Advance 4.** Every point of the repaired full regular locus lies in one of the genuine
bounded charts used to build the repaired atlas. -/
theorem exists_boundedRegularChart_at
    {G : Type uG} [Group G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (x : FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D) :
    ∃ a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J),
      x ∈ (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
        (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a).source := by
  exact (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularCover
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0).covers x

/-- **Advance 5.** Every repaired bounded chart is compatible with the repaired full preferred
atlas.  We record the specialization in the form used by the effective descent theorem. -/
theorem boundedRegularChart_compatible
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Finite G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J)) :
    let Sfull := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    IsTranslationChartFor Sfull.atlas
      (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
        (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a) := by
  dsimp
  exact BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart_isTranslationChartFor
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a

/-- **Advance 6.** Hence every repaired full regular point lies in a *compatible* genuine bounded
chart, with no choice of an auxiliary preferred chart required. -/
theorem exists_compatible_boundedRegularChart_at
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Finite G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (x : (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).Regular) :
    ∃ a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J),
      x ∈ (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
        (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a).source ∧
      IsTranslationChartFor
        (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
          (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).atlas
        (BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
          (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a) := by
  rcases exists_boundedRegularChart_at
      (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 x with ⟨a, hxa⟩
  refine ⟨a, hxa, ?_⟩
  exact boundedRegularChart_compatible
    (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly a

/-- **Advance 7.** Every point of the *actual* repaired reduced regular locus is contained in a
chart obtained by descending one genuine bounded full chart through an effective quotient sheet.
The descended chart is already compatible with the canonical reduced atlas. -/
theorem exists_descended_bounded_chart_at_reduced
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (x : (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).Regular) :
    let Sfull := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    let hreg := boundedPreservesRegular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    letI : MulAction H Sfull.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) Sfull hreg
    let htrans := boundedLocalTranslationOnRegular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    ∃ a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J),
      ∃ eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph Sfull.Regular
        (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) Sfull hreg),
      let y := canonicalRegularLift (H := H) Sfull hreg x
      let c := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
        (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a
      let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) Sfull hreg
      let χQ := QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart
        (H := H) c eQ
      let χR := TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart hcan χQ
      y ∈ c.source ∧ y ∈ eQ.source ∧
      (∀ z, z ∈ eQ.source →
        eQ z = quotientMap (H := H) (Y := Sfull.Regular) z) ∧
      x ∈ χR.source ∧
      IsTranslationChartFor
        (CanonicalReducedRegularAtlasEffective.atlas
          (H := H) Sfull hreg htrans) χR := by
  dsimp
  let Sfull := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) Sfull :=
    boundedPreservesRegular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let : MulAction H Sfull.Regular := regularMulAction (H := H) Sfull hreg
  let htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.IsLocalTranslationOnRegular (H := H) Sfull hreg :=
    boundedLocalTranslationOnRegular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let y : Sfull.Regular := canonicalRegularLift (H := H) Sfull hreg x
  rcases exists_compatible_boundedRegularChart_at
      (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly y with
    ⟨a, hya, hca⟩
  let c := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a
  rcases CanonicalReducedCompatibleChartExistenceEffective.exists_compatible_transported_chart_at
        (H := H) Sfull hreg htrans c hca hya with
    ⟨eQ, hyeQ, heQ, hcenter, hcompat⟩
  refine ⟨a, eQ, ?_⟩
  try dsimp [y, c]
  refine ⟨hya, hyeQ, heQ, ?_, hcompat⟩
  have hmap :
      (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) Sfull hreg)
          (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := Sfull.Regular) y) = x := by
    simpa [y] using canonicalRegularLift_maps_to (H := H) Sfull hreg x
  rw [hmap] at hcenter
  exact hcenter

/-- **Advance 8.** Compatibility immediately yields an open overlap on which the reduced preferred
chart is a literal translation of the descended repaired chart.  This is the precise transfer rule
needed for unit Lebesgue density. -/
theorem local_translation_compare_of_compatible
    {Y : Type uY} [TopologicalSpace Y]
    (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := Y))
    (χ : OpenPartialHomeomorph Y ℂ)
    (hχ : IsTranslationChartFor A χ)
    (x : Y) (hx : x ∈ χ.source) :
    ∃ U : Set Y, IsOpen U ∧ x ∈ U ∧
      U ⊆ χ.source ∩ (A.chartAt x).source ∧
      ∃ c : ℂ, ∀ z ∈ U, A.chartAt x z = χ z + c := by
  exact hχ x hx

/-- **Advance 9.** Therefore the descended repaired chart supplied at every reduced regular point
comes with an explicit open translation-comparison neighbourhood to the preferred reduced chart. -/
theorem exists_descended_bounded_chart_with_preferred_comparison
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (x : (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).Regular) :
    let Sfull := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    let hreg := boundedPreservesRegular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    letI : MulAction H Sfull.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) Sfull hreg
    let _htrans := boundedLocalTranslationOnRegular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    ∃ a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J),
      ∃ eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph Sfull.Regular
        (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) Sfull hreg),
      let c := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
        (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a
      let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) Sfull hreg
      let χQ := QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart
        (H := H) c eQ
      let χR := TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart hcan χQ
      x ∈ χR.source ∧
      ∃ U : Set Sred.Regular, IsOpen U ∧ x ∈ U ∧
        U ⊆ χR.source ∩ (Sred.atlas.chartAt x).source ∧
        ∃ t : ℂ, ∀ z ∈ U, Sred.atlas.chartAt x z = χR z + t := by
  dsimp
  rcases exists_descended_bounded_chart_at_reduced
      (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly x with
    ⟨a, eQ, _hyc, _hyeQ, _heQ, hxχ, hχ⟩
  refine ⟨a, eQ, hxχ, ?_⟩
  exact local_translation_compare_of_compatible
    (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).atlas
    _ hχ x hxχ

/-- Package the local comparison data needed by the next measure step. -/
def HasRepairedReducedTranslationComparison
    {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := X)) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : S.Regular,
    ∃ χ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ,
      x ∈ χ.source ∧ IsTranslationChartFor S.atlas χ ∧
      ∃ U : Set S.Regular, IsOpen U ∧ x ∈ U ∧
        U ⊆ χ.source ∩ (S.atlas.chartAt x).source ∧
        ∃ c : ℂ, ∀ z ∈ U, S.atlas.chartAt x z = χ z + c

/-- **Advance 10.** The chart-choice part of the remaining pointwise area problem is therefore
closed on the actual repaired reduced surface: at every regular point, one may work in a descended
genuine bounded chart and then transfer any local Lebesgue identity to the preferred reduced chart
by a pure translation. -/
theorem boundedReduced_hasRepairedReducedTranslationComparison
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite) :
    HasRepairedReducedTranslationComparison
      (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly) := by
  intro x
  rcases exists_descended_bounded_chart_at_reduced
      (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly x with
    ⟨_a, _eQ, _hyc, _hyeQ, _heQ, hxχ, hχ⟩
  refine ⟨_, hxχ, hχ, ?_⟩
  exact local_translation_compare_of_compatible _ _ hχ x hxχ

end RepairedReducedCompatibleChartCoverage


/-! ## 290. Updated boundary after closing reduced chart choice

The remaining determinant-one problem no longer contains any hidden chart-selection issue.  Every
point of the actual repaired reduced regular locus now has a chart obtained by descending a genuine
bounded interior/edge chart from the repaired full surface through an effective quotient sheet.
That chart contains the selected point and is compatible with the canonical reduced atlas.  Hence,
after shrinking, the preferred reduced chart is literally the descended chart plus a constant.

Accordingly the sole remaining local measure task is sharper than in Section 288: prove that the
normalized reduced area has unit Lebesgue density on the descended chart on some neighbourhood of
each point.  The normalized one-sheet identity of Section 280 already reduces this to restricting
one repaired full unit-density chart law from Section 273 to the chosen effective local sheet.
Once that restricted pushforward identity is formalized, translation invariance transfers unit
density to the preferred reduced chart, Section 284 supplies the arbitrary real-affine Jacobian,
and `scalesFlatArea_of_pointwise_local` closes the global scaling law.
-/

/-! ## 291. Aligning the normalized one-sheet identity with the descended repaired chart

Section 290 closed chart choice but still left one small mismatch between the quotient-measure
statement and the chart statement.  The normalized one-sheet theorem of Section 280 is formulated
for a refined fundamental set inside an arbitrary open set `O`, while the descended repaired chart
uses a specific quotient sheet `eQ` and a specific upstairs repaired chart `c`.  Before inserting
any interior/edge area law, we make the canonical choice

`O = c.source ∩ eQ.source`

and record all of the resulting source and coordinate identities.  The final theorem of this
section rewrites the normalized reduced restriction exactly as the pushforward of the upstairs
restricted area along the same parametrization on which the descended chart is literally `c`.
No area calculation is performed here; this section removes the last quotient/chart bookkeeping
mismatch before the physical-coordinate measure law is inserted.
-/

namespace ReducedOneSheetCoordinateBridge

open MeasureTheory
open TranslationAtlasGeometry
open ReducedQuotientTopology
open RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry
open RegularFiniteOrbitQuotient
open RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification
open RefinedFundamentalSheetInChart
open InvariantRegularAreaDescent
open NormalizedFiniteOrbitArea
open QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart
open TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport

universe uH uY

variable {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
variable [Group H] [Fintype H] [MulAction H Y]
variable [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y]
variable [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y]
variable [ContinuousConstSMul H Y]

variable (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
variable (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S)

@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def regularAction : MulAction H S.Regular :=
  regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg

noncomputable abbrev regularContinuousAction :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular :=
  RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg

omit [Fintype H] [T2Space Y] [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] in
/-- **Advance 1.** On any genuine local quotient sheet, an upstairs point lying in both the sheet
and a compatible chart maps into the source of the corresponding custom quotient chart.  This is
the source-level version of the identity `eQ.symm (q y) = y`. -/
theorem customQuotientChart_mem_on_sheet [Fintype H] [T2Space Y] [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (_heQ : ∀ z, z ∈ eQ.source →
      eQ z = quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)
    {y : S.Regular} (_hye : y ∈ eQ.source) (_hyc : y ∈ c.source),
    quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) y ∈
      (QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart
        (H := H) c eQ).source := by
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro c eQ heQ y hye hyc
  let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
  have hey : eQ y = q y := heQ y hye
  have hqt : q y ∈ eQ.target := by
    rw [← hey]
    exact eQ.mapsTo hye
  have hback : eQ.symm (q y) = y := by
    rw [← hey]
    exact eQ.left_inv hye
  change q y ∈ (eQ.symm.trans c).source
  rw [OpenPartialHomeomorph.trans_source]
  refine ⟨hqt, ?_⟩
  simpa [hback] using hyc

include hreg in
include hreg in
/-- **Advance 2.** After canonical transport to the actual reduced regular locus, the image of the
same upstairs point lies in the transported descended chart. -/
theorem transportedCustomChart_mem_on_sheet :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (_heQ : ∀ z, z ∈ eQ.source →
      eQ z = quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)
    {y : S.Regular} (_hye : y ∈ eQ.source) (_hyc : y ∈ c.source),
    let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
    let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg
    let χQ := QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart
      (H := H) c eQ
    let χR := TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart hcan χQ
    hcan (q y) ∈ χR.source := by
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro c eQ heQ y hye hyc
  dsimp
  have hq := customQuotientChart_mem_on_sheet
    (H := H) S hreg c eQ heQ hye hyc
  simpa [TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart] using hq

omit [Fintype H] [T2Space Y] [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] in
/-- **Advance 3.** More importantly, the transported descended coordinate is *literally* the
upstairs repaired coordinate on the sheet.  Thus no translation factor is introduced by quotient
descent itself; translations enter only when comparing with another compatible reduced chart. -/
theorem transportedCustomChart_apply_on_sheet [Fintype H] [T2Space Y] [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (_heQ : ∀ z, z ∈ eQ.source →
      eQ z = quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)
    {y : S.Regular} (_hye : y ∈ eQ.source),
    let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
    let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg
    let χQ := QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart
      (H := H) c eQ
    let χR := TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart hcan χQ
    χR (hcan (q y)) = c y := by
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro c eQ heQ y hye
  dsimp [TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart,
    QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart]
  let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
  have hey : eQ y = q y := heQ y hye
  simp only [Homeomorph.toOpenPartialHomeomorph_symm_apply, Homeomorph.symm_apply_apply]
  change c (eQ.symm (q y)) = c y
  rw [← hey]
  rw [eQ.left_inv hye]

/-- **Advance 4.** The canonical refined sheet attached to a descended repaired chart: intersect the
intrinsic finite-orbit fundamental neighbourhood with both the upstairs chart source and the chosen
local quotient-sheet source. -/
abbrev descendedChartRefinedSheet :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := S.Regular))
      (_htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) A)
      (_c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
      (_eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
      (_y : S.Regular), Set S.Regular := by
  try dsimp only
  letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro A htrans c eQ y
  exact refinedFundamentalSet A htrans y (c.source ∩ eQ.source)

omit [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] in
/-- **Advance 5.** If the centre belongs to the two sources, the chart-adapted refined sheet is an
open neighbourhood of the centre.  Hence it is a legitimate input to the normalized one-sheet
theorem. -/
theorem descendedChartRefinedSheet_open_mem [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := S.Regular))
    (htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) A)
    (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (y : S.Regular) (_hyc : y ∈ c.source) (_hye : y ∈ eQ.source),
    IsOpen (descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y) ∧
      y ∈ descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y := by
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro A htrans c eQ y hyc hye
  dsimp only [descendedChartRefinedSheet]
  exact refinedFundamentalSet_open_mem A htrans y (c.source ∩ eQ.source)
    (c.open_source.inter eQ.open_source) ⟨hyc, hye⟩

omit [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] in
/-- **Advance 6.** Every point of the chart-adapted refined sheet lies simultaneously in the
upstairs repaired chart and in the genuine local quotient sheet.  These are exactly the two source
facts repeatedly needed in the final measure calculation. -/
theorem descendedChartRefinedSheet_source_subsets [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := S.Regular))
    (htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) A)
    (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (y : S.Regular),
    descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y ⊆ c.source ∧
      descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y ⊆ eQ.source := by
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro A htrans c eQ y
  dsimp only [descendedChartRefinedSheet]
  have hsub := refinedFundamentalSet_subsets A htrans y (c.source ∩ eQ.source)
  constructor
  · intro z hz
    exact (hsub.2 hz).1
  · intro z hz
    exact (hsub.2 hz).2

/-- **Advance 7.** The entire reduced image of the chart-adapted refined sheet is contained in the
source of the transported descended chart. -/
theorem transportedCustomChart_contains_refined_image :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := S.Regular))
    (htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) A)
    (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (_heQ : ∀ z, z ∈ eQ.source →
      eQ z = quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)
    (y : S.Regular),
    let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
    let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg
    let χQ := QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart
      (H := H) c eQ
    let χR := TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart hcan χQ
    (fun z : S.Regular => hcan (q z)) ''
        descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y ⊆ χR.source := by
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro A htrans c eQ heQ y
  dsimp
  rintro _ ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩
  have hsubs := descendedChartRefinedSheet_source_subsets
    (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y
  exact transportedCustomChart_mem_on_sheet
    (H := H) S hreg c eQ heQ (hsubs.2 hz) (hsubs.1 hz)

/-- **Advance 8.** On that entire refined sheet the quotient parametrization followed by the
transported reduced chart is exactly the original upstairs coordinate.  This is the precise
coordinate commutative square required to push the upstairs Lebesgue law downstairs. -/
theorem transportedCustomChart_eq_upstairs_on_refinedSheet :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := S.Regular))
    (htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) A)
    (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (_heQ : ∀ z, z ∈ eQ.source →
      eQ z = quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)
    (y : S.Regular),
    let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
    let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg
    let χQ := QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart
      (H := H) c eQ
    let χR := TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart hcan χQ
    ∀ z ∈ descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y,
      χR (hcan (q z)) = c z := by
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro A htrans c eQ heQ y
  dsimp
  intro z hz
  have hsubs := descendedChartRefinedSheet_source_subsets
    (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y
  exact transportedCustomChart_apply_on_sheet
    (H := H) S hreg c eQ heQ (hsubs.2 hz)

omit [Fintype H] [T2Space Y] [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] in
/-- **Advance 9.** The image notation used by Section 280 is definitionally the image of the single
parametrization `z ↦ hcan (q z)`.  Recording this equality avoids a persistent nested-image mismatch
in the subsequent measure pushforward calculation. -/
theorem regularOrbitHomeomorph_image_quotientImage [Fintype H] [T2Space Y] [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y] :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (U : Set S.Regular),
    let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
    let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg
    hcan '' (q '' U) = (fun z : S.Regular => hcan (q z)) '' U := by
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro U
  dsimp
  ext w
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨v, ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z, ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩, rfl⟩

/-- **Advance 10.** The normalized one-sheet theorem is now aligned exactly with the descended
repaired chart.  On the reduced image of `descendedChartRefinedSheet`, normalized area is the
pushforward of *one* upstairs restricted sheet by `z ↦ hcan(q z)`; Advances 7--8 say that this
parametrization lands in the descended chart and that its chart coordinate is literally `c z`.
Thus the only remaining local measure input is the unit-density law for the restriction of
`restrictedArea S μ` to this refined subset of the genuine repaired chart. -/
theorem normalizedArea_restrict_descendedChartRefinedImage_eq :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    letI : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := S.Regular))
    (htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) A)
    (μ : Measure Y) [SMulInvariantMeasure H Y μ]
    (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (y : S.Regular) (_hyc : y ∈ c.source) (_hye : y ∈ eQ.source),
    let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
    let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg
    let U := descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y
    let φ := fun z : S.Regular => hcan (q z)
    (normalizedCanonicalRegularQuotientArea
      (H := H) S hreg A htrans μ).restrict (φ '' U) =
      Measure.map φ ((restrictedArea S μ).restrict U) := by
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  intro A htrans μ _instInvariant c eQ y hyc hye
  dsimp [descendedChartRefinedSheet]
  have h := normalizedReducedChart_has_oneSheet_density
    (H := H) S hreg A htrans μ y (c.source ∩ eQ.source)
      (c.open_source.inter eQ.open_source) ⟨hyc, hye⟩
  dsimp at h
  rw [_root_.McMullen313Strict.ReducedOneSheetCoordinateBridge.regularOrbitHomeomorph_image_quotientImage (H := H) S hreg] at h
  simpa using h

end ReducedOneSheetCoordinateBridge


/-! ## 292. Updated boundary after aligning quotient normalization and descended coordinates

The normalized-area theorem and the repaired descended chart now use exactly the same local sheet.
For a genuine upstairs repaired chart `c` and the selected effective quotient sheet `eQ`, the
canonical refinement is

`refinedFundamentalSet A htrans y (c.source ∩ eQ.source)`.

It is open, contains the centre, lies in both sources, and its reduced image lies in the transported
descended chart.  On every point of this refined sheet the transported reduced coordinate is
literally the upstairs coordinate `c`; there is no quotient-induced translation or scalar.  Most
importantly, the normalized reduced measure restricted to that same image is exactly the pushforward
of the upstairs restricted area of that sheet.

Therefore the determinant-one branch has reached a single concrete measure restriction problem:
prove that restricting either repaired physical full-chart unit-density theorem of Section 273 to
an arbitrary open subset of the chart source preserves unit density in the same coordinate.  Once
that restriction lemma is specialized to the bounded interior/edge alternatives of the selected
`BoundedIndex`, Advance 10 above and the coordinate commutative square give unit Lebesgue density on
the descended reduced chart.  Translation comparison from Section 290 and the real-affine Jacobian
of Section 284 can then produce `PointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea`.
-/

/-! ## 293. Arbitrary-restriction localization of the repaired physical chart laws

Section 292 reduced the normalized reduced-area problem to a restriction of one genuine repaired
full chart to the refined quotient sheet.  The whole-chart unit-density identities of Section 273
are not by themselves enough: one must justify that pushing forward a restricted measure through
the chart really is the restriction of the pushed-forward measure.  This is automatic for a
measurable embedding, but the injectivity is essential and should not be hidden in a rewrite.

We first prove the general measurable-embedding localization lemma.  We then apply it twice to each
repaired branch: once to the intrinsic parametrization into the full unfolding and once to the
physical coordinate into `ℂ`.  Consequently an arbitrary measurable intrinsic subpatch carries one
and the same restricted measure whose ambient realization is canonical full area and whose physical
realization is literal Lebesgue measure.  This is exactly the two-sided bridge needed for the
refined sheet of Section 291.
-/

namespace RepairedPhysicalChartRestriction

open MeasureTheory
open CompactPlanarPolygonArea
open FiniteCopyPolygonArea
open PolygonQuotientFlatArea
open FullCopyUnfolding
open FullCopyUnfoldingTopology
open FullInteriorFlatCharts
open PackagedFullInteriorMeasure
open BoundedEdgeWindowRepair
