    exact boundedFullFlatEdgeChartAt_windowTargetToFullAt
      (G := G) H P₀ D V L hreflect p

/-- **Advance 10.** Unified closure of the arbitrary-restriction step.  In both repaired branches,
the same intrinsic restricted measure has two exact realizations: canonical full area on the
corresponding full-unfolding subpatch and unit Lebesgue measure on the corresponding physical
coordinate image.  Hence Section 292's remaining issue is no longer a restriction theorem; it is
only the conversion between a refined subset of the regular subtype and the intrinsic parameter
subset of the selected bounded chart. -/
theorem repairedPhysicalSubpatch_measure_bridges
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ)) :
    (∀ (J : InteriorPatch (H := H) D V) (g : G)
        (T : Set {p : P₀.carrier // p ∈ J.U}), MeasurableSet T →
      Measure.map (copyPatchMap (H := H) D g J.U)
          ((fullInteriorCoordinateMeasure (G := G) H P₀ D V J g).restrict T) =
        (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D).restrict
          (copyPatchMap (H := H) D g J.U '' T) ∧
      Measure.map (interiorDevelopingMap (H := H) D V g J.U)
          ((fullInteriorCoordinateMeasure (G := G) H P₀ D V J g).restrict T) =
        (volume : Measure ℂ).restrict
          (interiorDevelopingMap (H := H) D V g J.U '' T)) ∧
    (∀ {e : E} {W : HalfPlaneWindow} {g : G}
        (L : WindowFlatLocalEdgeParam (H := H) D V W g e)
        (_hreflect : D.reflect e ≠ 1)
        (T : Set W.FoldedPoint), MeasurableSet T →
      Measure.map (windowTargetToFullAt (G := G) H P₀ D
          L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam g)
          ((fullEdgeCoordinateMeasureAt (G := G) H P₀ D
            L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam g).restrict T) =
        (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D).restrict
          (windowTargetToFullAt (G := G) H P₀ D
            L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam g '' T) ∧
      Measure.map (physicalFoldedMap (H := H) (P₀ := P₀) (D := D) V L)
          ((fullEdgeCoordinateMeasureAt (G := G) H P₀ D
            L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam g).restrict T) =
        (volume : Measure ℂ).restrict
          (physicalFoldedMap (H := H) (P₀ := P₀) (D := D) V L '' T)) := by
  constructor
  · intro J g T hT
    exact ⟨map_copyPatchMap_restrict_fullInteriorCoordinateMeasure
      (G := G) H P₀ D V J g hT,
      map_interiorDevelopingMap_restrict_fullInteriorCoordinateMeasure
        (G := G) H P₀ D V hdev J g hT⟩
  · intro e W g L hreflect T hT
    exact ⟨_root_.McMullen313Strict.RepairedPhysicalChartRestriction.map_windowTargetToFullAt_restrict_fullEdgeCoordinateMeasureAt
      (G := G) H P₀ D L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam hreflect hT,
      map_physicalFoldedMap_restrict_fullEdgePhysicalCoordinateMeasureAt
        (G := G) H P₀ D V hdev L hreflect hT⟩

end RepairedPhysicalChartRestriction


/-! ## 294. Updated boundary after closing arbitrary physical-subpatch localization

The restriction gap isolated in Section 292 is now closed at the intrinsic-chart level.  The key
new general lemma is that `Measure.map` commutes with restriction along a measurable embedding;
injectivity is used explicitly, so no unsupported rewrite from a whole-chart law to a subchart law
remains.  Applying this to both embeddings associated to each repaired chart shows the following.

For every measurable interior subpatch `T`, one intrinsic restricted measure pushes to canonical
`fullArea` on the copy-patch image and simultaneously pushes to ordinary Lebesgue measure on the
developed-coordinate image.  The identical two-sided statement holds for every measurable bounded
edge subpatch at every copy label, with the physical affine seam coordinate.  Advances 8--9 also
identify those Euclidean images literally with the images under the actual repaired ambient charts.

Thus the determinant-one branch no longer needs any new interior/edge Jacobian or arbitrary-set
localization argument.  The remaining local bridge is now purely a change of parameter space:
given the refined open set `U` of Section 291 inside the *regular subtype* and the selected bounded
index `a`, pull `U` back through the intrinsic interior or folded-window parametrization, prove that
this intrinsic preimage is measurable, and identify its ambient image with `Subtype.val '' U`.
The two-sided bridge above will then give unit density for `restrictedArea` on `U`; Section 291 will
immediately descend that identity to normalized reduced area.
-/

/-! ## 295. From intrinsic repaired subpatches to regular-chart Lebesgue mass

Section 294 localized the two physical repaired chart laws to arbitrary measurable subsets of the
intrinsic parameter spaces.  The remaining mismatch is that the normalized quotient construction
selects an open subset of the *regular subtype*.  We now eliminate that mismatch without treating an
`OpenPartialHomeomorph` as a globally measurable map outside its source.

The robust local notion is setwise: on a subset `U` of a translation chart, every measurable
`A ⊆ U` has surface mass equal to planar Lebesgue mass of its chart image.  For each bounded interior
or edge chart we pull `Subtype.val '' A` back through the genuine intrinsic open embedding, apply the
two pushforward identities of Section 293, and compare total masses.  This yields a unified theorem
for every repaired bounded regular chart and hence for every refined quotient sheet contained in
such a chart.
-/

namespace RepairedRegularChartUnitDensity

open MeasureTheory
open CompactPlanarPolygonArea
open FiniteCopyPolygonArea
open PolygonQuotientFlatArea
open FullCopyUnfolding
open FullInteriorFlatCharts
open PackagedFullInteriorMeasure
open BoundedEdgeWindowRepair
open BoundedEdgeWindowFullBridge
open BoundedEdgeWindowTopologyBridge
open ArbitraryCopyBoundedEdgeMeasure
open RepairedPhysicalChartAreaNormalization
open RepairedPhysicalChartRestriction
open BoundedRegularAtlasRepair
open BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction
open InvariantRegularAreaDescent
open RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry
open ReducedOneSheetCoordinateBridge

universe uA uB uC uG uE uI uJ

/-- **Advance 1.** If one measure on a parameter space pushes forward to restrictions of two
ambient measures, then the two target restrictions have the same total mass.  This is the exact
setwise extraction used below and avoids any global measurability assertion for a partial chart. -/
theorem mass_eq_of_two_restricted_pushforwards
    {A : Type uA} {B : Type uB} {C : Type uC}
    [MeasurableSpace A] [MeasurableSpace B] [MeasurableSpace C]
    (f : A → B) (g : A → C) (hf : Measurable f) (hg : Measurable g)
    (ρ : Measure A) (μ : Measure B) (ν : Measure C)
    (V : Set B) (W : Set C)
    (hfmap : Measure.map f ρ = μ.restrict V)
    (hgmap : Measure.map g ρ = ν.restrict W) :
    μ V = ν W := by
  have h1 := congrArg (fun m : Measure B => m Set.univ) hfmap
  have h2 := congrArg (fun m : Measure C => m Set.univ) hgmap
  rw [Measure.map_apply hf MeasurableSet.univ] at h1
  rw [Measure.map_apply hg MeasurableSet.univ] at h2
  have h1' : ρ Set.univ = μ V := by
    simpa [Measure.restrict_apply] using h1
  have h2' : ρ Set.univ = ν W := by
    simpa [Measure.restrict_apply] using h2
  exact h1'.symm.trans h2'

/-- **Advance 2.** Restricting ambient area to the regular subtype and then to a measurable regular
set, followed by the subtype inclusion, is literally ambient area restricted to the subtype image.
This packages the regular/ambient measure conversion independently of any polygon chart. -/
theorem map_subtypeVal_restrict_restrictedArea
    {Y : Type uB} [TopologicalSpace Y]
    [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y)) (μ : Measure Y)
    {U : Set S.Regular} (hU : MeasurableSet U) :
    Measure.map (fun x : S.Regular => (x : Y))
        ((restrictedArea S μ).restrict U) =
      μ.restrict (Subtype.val '' U) := by
  have hOpen := S.isOpen_regular.isOpenEmbedding_subtypeVal
  have hEmb : MeasurableEmbedding (fun x : S.Regular => (x : Y)) :=
    hOpen.isEmbedding.measurableEmbedding hOpen.isOpen_range.measurableSet
  simpa [restrictedArea] using
    (RepairedPhysicalChartRestriction.map_restrict_comap_measurableEmbedding
      (fun x : S.Regular => (x : Y)) hEmb
      hOpen.isOpen_range.measurableSet μ hU)

/-- **Advance 3.** Pulling a target subset back through any map and pushing it forward again recovers
that subset as soon as it lies in the range.  No injectivity is needed.  This is the set-theoretic
bridge from a regular-subtype subset to the intrinsic interior/folded parameter subset. -/
theorem image_preimage_eq_of_subset_range
    {A : Type uA} {B : Type uB} (f : A → B) (V : Set B)
    (hV : V ⊆ Set.range f) :
    f '' (f ⁻¹' V) = V := by
  ext y
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact hx
  · intro hy
    rcases hV hy with ⟨x, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨x, hy, rfl⟩

variable {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
variable (H : Subgroup G)
variable {E : Type uE}
variable (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
variable [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
variable (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
variable [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
variable [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
variable [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
variable (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
variable {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
variable (CI : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
variable (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
variable (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)

local instance groupBorelMeasurableSpace : MeasurableSpace G := borel G
local instance groupBorelSpace : BorelSpace G := ⟨rfl⟩

noncomputable local instance fullBorelMeasurableSpace :
    MeasurableSpace (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D) :=
  borel (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)

local instance fullBorelSpace :
    BorelSpace (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D) := ⟨rfl⟩

omit [Fintype G] [ContinuousConstSMul ↥H ↑P₀.carrier] in
/-- **Advance 4.** The image of a subset under a repaired *regular* chart is exactly the image of
its ambient subtype image under the corresponding repaired ambient bounded chart.  Thus passing to
the regular subtype changes neither coordinates nor coordinate images. -/
theorem regularChart_image_eq_boundedChart_image_val [Fintype G] [ContinuousConstSMul ↥H ↑P₀.carrier]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier)
    (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J))
    (A : Set (FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D)) :
    regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a '' A =
      boundedChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect a ''
        (Subtype.val '' A) := by
  ext z
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨(x : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D), ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    symm
    exact regularChart_apply
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a x
  · rintro ⟨y, ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨x, hx, ?_⟩
    exact regularChart_apply
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a x

/-- **Advance 5.** Interior parameterization of a measurable regular-chart subpatch.  The pulled
back intrinsic set is measurable; its copy image is exactly the ambient subtype image; and its
physical developed image is exactly the regular-chart image. -/
theorem interior_regularSubpatch_parameter_bridge
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier)
    (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (g : G) (i : I)
    {A : Set (FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D)}
    (hA : MeasurableSet A)
    (hAsrc : A ⊆
      (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inl (g, i))).source) :
    let J₀ := CI.patch i
    let f := copyPatchMap (H := H) D g J₀.U
    let k := interiorDevelopingMap (H := H) D V g J₀.U
    let T := f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)
    MeasurableSet T ∧
      f '' T = Subtype.val '' A ∧
      k '' T =
        regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inl (g, i)) '' A := by
  dsimp
  let J₀ := CI.patch i
  let f := copyPatchMap (H := H) D g J₀.U
  have hOpenVal :=
    (regularSet_isOpen_bounded (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect).isOpenEmbedding_subtypeVal
  have hValEmb : MeasurableEmbedding
      (fun x : FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D =>
        (x : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)) :=
    hOpenVal.isEmbedding.measurableEmbedding hOpenVal.isOpen_range.measurableSet
  have hAval : MeasurableSet
      (Subtype.val '' A : Set (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)) :=
    hValEmb.measurableSet_image.mpr hA
  have hfOpen := copyPatchMap_isOpenEmbedding
    (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D g J₀.isOpen_U J₀.noEdge_U
  have hfEmb : MeasurableEmbedding f :=
    hfOpen.isEmbedding.measurableEmbedding hfOpen.isOpen_range.measurableSet
  have hT : MeasurableSet (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)) :=
    hAval.preimage hfEmb.measurable
  have hRange : Subtype.val '' A ⊆ Set.range f := by
    rintro _ ⟨x, hxA, rfl⟩
    have hxsrc := hAsrc hxA
    have hxamb := (mem_regularChart_source_iff
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0
      (Sum.inl (g, i)) x).1 hxsrc
    change (x : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D) ∈
      (J₀.fullInteriorChart (G := G) (H := H) D V g).source at hxamb
    rw [J₀.fullInteriorChart_source (G := G) (H := H) D V g] at hxamb
    exact hxamb
  have hImage : f '' (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)) = Subtype.val '' A :=
    image_preimage_eq_of_subset_range f (Subtype.val '' A) hRange
  have hPhys := fullInteriorChart_image_copyPatchMap
    (G := G) H P₀ D V J₀ g (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A))
  have hRegImg := regularChart_image_eq_boundedChart_image_val
    (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0
      (Sum.inl (g, i)) A
  have hCoord :
      interiorDevelopingMap (H := H) D V g J₀.U ''
          (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)) =
        regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inl (g, i)) '' A := by
    rw [hRegImg]
    change interiorDevelopingMap (H := H) D V g J₀.U ''
        (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)) =
      (J₀.fullInteriorChart (G := G) (H := H) D V g) ''
        (Subtype.val '' A)
    conv_rhs => rw [← hImage]
    exact hPhys.symm
  exact ⟨hT, hImage, hCoord⟩

/-- **Advance 6.** Every measurable subset of an interior repaired regular chart has exactly unit
Lebesgue mass in that chart coordinate.  This is a setwise statement, so no behavior of the partial
chart outside its source is invoked. -/
theorem interior_regularChart_unitLebesgue_mass
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ))
    [Finite G]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier)
    (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (g : G) (i : I)
    {A : Set (FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D)}
    (hA : MeasurableSet A)
    (hAsrc : A ⊆
      (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inl (g, i))).source) :
    restrictedArea
        (surface (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
        (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D) A =
      (volume : Measure ℂ)
        (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inl (g, i)) '' A) := by
  let J₀ := CI.patch i
  let f := copyPatchMap (H := H) D g J₀.U
  let k := interiorDevelopingMap (H := H) D V g J₀.U
  let T := f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)
  rcases interior_regularSubpatch_parameter_bridge
      (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 g i hA hAsrc with
    ⟨hT, hImage, hCoord⟩
  have hfmap := map_copyPatchMap_restrict_fullInteriorCoordinateMeasure
    (G := G) H P₀ D V J₀ g hT
  have hkmap := map_interiorDevelopingMap_restrict_fullInteriorCoordinateMeasure
    (G := G) H P₀ D V hdev J₀ g hT
  have hfOpen := copyPatchMap_isOpenEmbedding
    (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D g J₀.isOpen_U J₀.noEdge_U
  have hkOpen := FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorPatch.developedCopy_isOpenEmbedding (H := H) D V J₀ g
  have hmass := mass_eq_of_two_restricted_pushforwards
    f k hfOpen.continuous.measurable hkOpen.continuous.measurable
    ((fullInteriorCoordinateMeasure (G := G) H P₀ D V J₀ g).restrict T)
    (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D) (volume : Measure ℂ)
    (f '' T) (k '' T) hfmap hkmap
  rw [hImage, hCoord] at hmass
  have hrestrict := restrictedArea_apply
    (surface (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
    (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D) hA
  exact hrestrict.trans hmass

/-- **Advance 7.** Bounded-edge analogue of Advance 5.  Pulling a measurable regular-chart subset
back through the folded target embedding gives a measurable intrinsic folded set whose full image
and physical-coordinate image are exactly the ambient and regular-chart images. -/
theorem edge_regularSubpatch_parameter_bridge
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier)
    (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (j : J)
    {A : Set (FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D)}
    (hA : MeasurableSet A)
    (hAsrc : A ⊆
      (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inr j)).source) :
    let L := CE.patch j
    let f := windowTargetToFullAt (G := G) H P₀ D
      L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam (CE.copy j)
    let k := physicalFoldedMap (H := H) (P₀ := P₀) (D := D) V L
    let T := f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)
    MeasurableSet T ∧
      f '' T = Subtype.val '' A ∧
      k '' T =
        regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inr j) '' A := by
  dsimp
  let L := CE.patch j
  let f := windowTargetToFullAt (G := G) H P₀ D
    L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam (CE.copy j)
  have hOpenVal :=
    (regularSet_isOpen_bounded (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect).isOpenEmbedding_subtypeVal
  have hValEmb : MeasurableEmbedding
      (fun x : FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D =>
        (x : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)) :=
    hOpenVal.isEmbedding.measurableEmbedding hOpenVal.isOpen_range.measurableSet
  have hAval : MeasurableSet
      (Subtype.val '' A : Set (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)) :=
    hValEmb.measurableSet_image.mpr hA
  have hfOpen := windowTargetToFullAt_isOpenEmbedding
    (G := G) H P₀ D L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam
      (CE.copy j) (hreflect (CE.edge j))
  have hfEmb : MeasurableEmbedding f :=
    hfOpen.isEmbedding.measurableEmbedding hfOpen.isOpen_range.measurableSet
  have hT : MeasurableSet (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)) :=
    hAval.preimage hfEmb.measurable
  have hRange : Subtype.val '' A ⊆ Set.range f := by
    rintro _ ⟨x, hxA, rfl⟩
    have hxsrc := hAsrc hxA
    have hxamb := (mem_regularChart_source_iff
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0
      (Sum.inr j) x).1 hxsrc
    change (x : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D) ∈
      (boundedFullFlatEdgeChartAt (G := G) (H := H) D V
        L (hreflect (CE.edge j))).source at hxamb
    rw [BoundedRegularAtlasCompatibility.boundedFullFlatEdgeChartAt_source
      (G := G) (H := H) D V L (hreflect (CE.edge j))] at hxamb
    rcases hxamb with ⟨q, hq⟩
    refine ⟨(CE.window j).seamEquiv q, ?_⟩
    simpa [f, windowTargetToFullAt] using hq
  have hImage : f '' (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)) = Subtype.val '' A :=
    image_preimage_eq_of_subset_range f (Subtype.val '' A) hRange
  have hPhys := boundedFullFlatEdgeChartAt_image_windowTargetToFullAt
    (G := G) H P₀ D V L (hreflect (CE.edge j))
      (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A))
  have hRegImg := regularChart_image_eq_boundedChart_image_val
    (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inr j) A
  have hCoord :
      physicalFoldedMap (H := H) (P₀ := P₀) (D := D) V L ''
          (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)) =
        regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inr j) '' A := by
    rw [hRegImg]
    change physicalFoldedMap (H := H) (P₀ := P₀) (D := D) V L ''
        (f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)) =
      (boundedFullFlatEdgeChartAt (G := G) (H := H) D V
        L (hreflect (CE.edge j))) '' (Subtype.val '' A)
    conv_rhs => rw [← hImage]
    exact hPhys.symm
  exact ⟨hT, hImage, hCoord⟩

/-- **Advance 8.** Every measurable subset of a bounded-edge repaired regular chart has unit
Lebesgue mass in the repaired physical coordinate, with the same canonical full area as in the
interior branch. -/
theorem edge_regularChart_unitLebesgue_mass
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ))
    [Finite G]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier)
    (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (j : J)
    {A : Set (FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D)}
    (hA : MeasurableSet A)
    (hAsrc : A ⊆
      (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inr j)).source) :
    restrictedArea
        (surface (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
        (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D) A =
      (volume : Measure ℂ)
        (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 (Sum.inr j) '' A) := by
  let L := CE.patch j
  let f := windowTargetToFullAt (G := G) H P₀ D
    L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam (CE.copy j)
  let k := physicalFoldedMap (H := H) (P₀ := P₀) (D := D) V L
  let T := f ⁻¹' (Subtype.val '' A)
  rcases edge_regularSubpatch_parameter_bridge
      (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 j hA hAsrc with
    ⟨hT, hImage, hCoord⟩
  have hfmap := map_windowTargetToFullAt_restrict_fullEdgeCoordinateMeasureAt
    (G := G) (g := CE.copy j) H P₀ D L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam
      (hreflect (CE.edge j)) hT
  have hkmap := map_physicalFoldedMap_restrict_fullEdgePhysicalCoordinateMeasureAt
    (G := G) H P₀ D V hdev L (hreflect (CE.edge j)) hT
  have hfOpen := windowTargetToFullAt_isOpenEmbedding
    (G := G) H P₀ D L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam
      (CE.copy j) (hreflect (CE.edge j))
  have hkOpen := physicalFoldedMap_isOpenEmbedding
    (G := G) H P₀ D V L
  have hmass := mass_eq_of_two_restricted_pushforwards
    f k hfOpen.continuous.measurable hkOpen.continuous.measurable
    ((fullEdgeCoordinateMeasureAt (G := G) H P₀ D
      L.toTopologicalWindowLocalEdgeParam (CE.copy j)).restrict T)
    (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D) (volume : Measure ℂ)
    (f '' T) (k '' T) hfmap hkmap
  rw [hImage, hCoord] at hmass
  have hrestrict := restrictedArea_apply
    (surface (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
    (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D) hA
  exact hrestrict.trans hmass

/-- **Advance 9.** The interior/edge dichotomy is now erased at the regular-atlas level.  For every
repaired bounded chart index and every measurable subset of its source, canonical restricted full
area is literally unit Lebesgue mass of the regular-chart image. -/
theorem boundedRegularChart_unitLebesgue_mass
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ))
    [Finite G]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier)
    (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J))
    {A : Set (FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D)}
    (hA : MeasurableSet A)
    (hAsrc : A ⊆
      (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 a).source) :
    restrictedArea
        (surface (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
        (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D) A =
      (volume : Measure ℂ)
        (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 a '' A) := by
  cases a with
  | inl gi =>
      rcases gi with ⟨g, i⟩
      exact interior_regularChart_unitLebesgue_mass
        (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect hdev
          g0 p0 hp0 hpoly g i hA hAsrc
  | inr j =>
      exact edge_regularChart_unitLebesgue_mass
        (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect hdev
          g0 p0 hp0 hpoly j hA hAsrc

/-- Setwise unit-density on a local chart region.  This formulation deliberately asks only about
measurable subsets lying inside the region, so the partial chart is never used as a globally
measurable function outside its source. -/
def UnitLebesgueMassOn
    {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    (μ : Measure X) (χ : OpenPartialHomeomorph X ℂ) (U : Set X) : Prop :=
  ∀ A : Set X, MeasurableSet A → A ⊆ U →
    μ A = (volume : Measure ℂ) (χ '' A)

/-- **Advance 10.** Any open subset of one repaired bounded regular chart, in particular the refined
sheet selected in Section 291, inherits a complete setwise unit-Lebesgue law.  Thus the remaining
quotient step no longer needs to know whether the selected full chart was interior or edge. -/
theorem boundedRegularChart_unitLebesgue_on_openSubset
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ))
    [Finite G]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier)
    (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (a : BoundedIndex (G := G) (I := I) (J := J))
    (U : Set (FullRegularFlatChartRestriction.Regular (G := G) (H := H) D))
    (hUopen : IsOpen U)
    (hUsrc : U ⊆
      (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 a).source) :
    IsOpen U ∧
      UnitLebesgueMassOn
        (restrictedArea
          (surface (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
            g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
          (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D))
        (regularChart (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect
          g0 p0 hp0 a) U := by
  refine ⟨hUopen, ?_⟩
  intro A hA hAU
  exact boundedRegularChart_unitLebesgue_mass
    (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect hdev
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly a hA (Set.Subset.trans hAU hUsrc)

end RepairedRegularChartUnitDensity


/-! ## 296. Updated boundary after closing the regular-subtype parameter mismatch

The intrinsic-parameter restriction theorem of Section 293 has now been transferred all the way to
the actual repaired full regular atlas.  The proof never assumes that an `OpenPartialHomeomorph` is
measurable outside its source.  Instead, for a measurable regular subset `A` contained in one
bounded chart, its ambient subtype image is pulled back through the genuine interior or folded-window
open embedding.  The two Section 293 pushforwards then identify the *same* intrinsic restricted
measure both with canonical full area on `Subtype.val '' A` and with planar Lebesgue measure on the
physical coordinate image.  Equality of total masses gives

`restrictedArea fullArea A = volume (regularChart a '' A)`.

This statement is unified over the whole `BoundedIndex`; no interior/edge case remains in subsequent
arguments.  Moreover every open subregion of a repaired regular chart carries this setwise unit
Lebesgue law.  Since Section 291's `descendedChartRefinedSheet` is open and contained in its chosen
upstairs repaired chart, the full-side input required by normalized one-sheet descent is now closed.

The next remaining local step is entirely downstairs: use Section 291's exact one-sheet measure
identity and the equality `χR (hcan (q z)) = c z` on the refined sheet to transfer the setwise unit
Lebesgue law to the transported descended reduced chart.  After that, the translation comparison of
Section 290 moves the law to the preferred reduced chart, and the real-affine Jacobian theorem can be
inserted directly into the pointwise scaling argument.
-/

/-! ## 297. Descent of unit Lebesgue density to the preferred reduced chart

Section 296 gives a setwise unit-Lebesgue law on every measurable subset of an arbitrary open
subregion of a repaired bounded full regular chart.  Section 291 gives the normalized one-sheet
identity on the reduced image of the same refined sheet, together with the exact coordinate
identity saying that the transported descended chart equals the upstairs chart after quotienting.

The remaining argument is purely functorial.  We first prove a general one-sheet pushforward lemma
for setwise unit density.  We then show that the canonical reduced parametrization is measurable,
that the refined reduced image is an open neighbourhood of its centre, and specialize the general
lemma to the normalized quotient area.  Finally we transfer the resulting density from the
descended repaired chart to the preferred reduced chart by the translation overlap.  No new area,
Jacobian, orbit-degree, or interior/edge calculation occurs in this section.
-/

namespace ReducedPreferredUnitDensityClosure

open PolygonQuotientFlatArea

open MeasureTheory
open TranslationAtlasGeometry
open ReducedQuotientTopology
open RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry
open RegularFiniteOrbitQuotient
open RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification
open RefinedFundamentalSheetInChart
open InvariantRegularAreaDescent
open NormalizedFiniteOrbitArea
open QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart
open TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport
open ReducedOneSheetCoordinateBridge
open RepairedRegularChartUnitDensity
open RepairedReducedCompatibleChartCoverage
open BoundedRegularAtlasRepair
open BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction
open BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation
open NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure
open TranslationOverlapLebesgueConsistency
open FullCopyUnfolding
open FullRegularFlatChartRestriction
open AffineFlatAreaScaling

universe uX uZ uH uY uG uE uI uJ

/-- **Advance 1.** General one-sheet descent of setwise unit Lebesgue density.  If the target
measure restricted to `φ '' U` is the pushforward of one source sheet, the source has unit density
in chart `c`, and the target chart `χ` satisfies `χ (φ x) = c x` on the sheet, then the target has
unit density on `φ '' U`.  No injectivity of `φ` outside the chosen sheet is required. -/
theorem unitLebesgueMassOn_of_oneSheet_pushforward
    {X : Type uX} {Z : Type uZ}
    [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    [TopologicalSpace Z] [MeasurableSpace Z]
    (μ : Measure X) (ν : Measure Z)
    (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph X ℂ)
    (χ : OpenPartialHomeomorph Z ℂ)
    (U : Set X) (hU : MeasurableSet U)
    (φ : X → Z) (hφ : Measurable φ)
    (hmeasure : ν.restrict (φ '' U) = Measure.map φ (μ.restrict U))
    (hunit : UnitLebesgueMassOn μ c U)
    (hcoord : ∀ x ∈ U, χ (φ x) = c x) :
    UnitLebesgueMassOn ν χ (φ '' U) := by
  intro A hA hAsub
  let T : Set X := φ ⁻¹' A ∩ U
  have hT : MeasurableSet T := (hA.preimage hφ).inter hU
  have hTU : T ⊆ U := by
    intro x hx
    exact hx.2
  have hrest : (ν.restrict (φ '' U)) A = ν A := by
    rw [Measure.restrict_apply hA]
    rw [Set.inter_eq_left.mpr hAsub]
  have hmap : Measure.map φ (μ.restrict U) A = (μ.restrict U) (φ ⁻¹' A) :=
    Measure.map_apply hφ hA
  have hsource : (μ.restrict U) (φ ⁻¹' A) = μ T := by
    rw [Measure.restrict_apply (hA.preimage hφ)]
    try rfl
  have hmass : μ T = (volume : Measure ℂ) (c '' T) := hunit T hT hTU
  have himage : c '' T = χ '' A := by
    ext w
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨x, hxT, rfl⟩
      have hxA : φ x ∈ A := hxT.1
      have hxU : x ∈ U := hxT.2
      refine ⟨φ x, hxA, ?_⟩
      exact hcoord x hxU
    · rintro ⟨z, hzA, rfl⟩
      have hzV : z ∈ φ '' U := hAsub hzA
      rcases hzV with ⟨x, hxU, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨x, ?_, ?_⟩
      · exact ⟨hzA, hxU⟩
      · exact (hcoord x hxU).symm
  calc
    ν A = (ν.restrict (φ '' U)) A := hrest.symm
    _ = Measure.map φ (μ.restrict U) A := by rw [hmeasure]
    _ = (μ.restrict U) (φ ⁻¹' A) := hmap
    _ = μ T := hsource
    _ = (volume : Measure ℂ) (c '' T) := hmass
    _ = (volume : Measure ℂ) (χ '' A) := by rw [himage]

/-- **Advance 2.** The canonical parametrization from the full regular locus to the actual reduced
regular locus, `z ↦ hcan (q z)`, is measurable.  This is the only analytic hypothesis needed by the
general one-sheet descent lemma. -/
theorem canonicalReducedParam_measurable
    {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
    [Group H] [Fintype H] [MulAction H Y]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y] [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H Y]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
    (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S) :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    Measurable (fun z : S.Regular =>
      (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg)
        (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)) := by
  try dsimp only

  let : MulAction H S.Regular := regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular :=
    regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  exact (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg).measurable.comp
    (quotientMap_continuous (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)).measurable

/-- **Advance 3.** The reduced image of a chart-adapted refined sheet is open.  Openness comes from
the genuine open finite-orbit quotient map followed by the canonical homeomorphism; it does not
require the auxiliary sheet chart `eQ` to be globally surjective or globally equal to the quotient
map. -/
theorem descendedRefinedImage_open
    {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
    [Group H] [Fintype H] [MulAction H Y]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H Y]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
    (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S) :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := S.Regular))
    (htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) A)
    (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (y : S.Regular) (_hyc : y ∈ c.source) (_hye : y ∈ eQ.source),
    IsOpen ((fun z : S.Regular =>
      (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg)
        (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)) ''
      descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y) := by
  try dsimp only
  intro A htrans c eQ y hyc hye

  let : MulAction H S.Regular := regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  let : ContinuousConstSMul H S.Regular :=
    regularContinuousConstSMul (H := H) S hreg
  let U := descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y
  have hUopen : IsOpen U :=
    (descendedChartRefinedSheet_open_mem
      (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y hyc hye).1
  have hQopen : IsOpen (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) '' U) :=
    quotientMap_isOpenMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) U hUopen
  have hEopen : IsOpen
      ((regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg) ''
        (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) '' U)) :=
    (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg).isOpenMap _ hQopen
  rw [_root_.McMullen313Strict.ReducedOneSheetCoordinateBridge.regularOrbitHomeomorph_image_quotientImage (H := H) S hreg] at hEopen
  exact hEopen

/-- **Advance 4.** The centre of the refined upstairs sheet maps to the centre of its reduced image.
This elementary membership statement is kept explicit because it is what later guarantees that the
unit-density neighbourhood survives intersection with the preferred-chart comparison neighbourhood. -/
theorem canonicalReducedParam_mem_descendedRefinedImage
    {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
    [Group H] [Fintype H] [MulAction H Y]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H Y]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
    (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S) :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := S.Regular))
    (htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) A)
    (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (y : S.Regular) (_hyc : y ∈ c.source) (_hye : y ∈ eQ.source),
    (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg)
        (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) y) ∈
      (fun z : S.Regular =>
        (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg)
          (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)) ''
        descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y := by
  try dsimp only
  intro A htrans c eQ y hyc hye

  have hyU :=
    (descendedChartRefinedSheet_open_mem
      (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y hyc hye).2
  exact ⟨y, hyU, rfl⟩

/-- **Advance 5.** Specialization of Advance 1 to the normalized finite-orbit measure.  Once an
upstairs refined sheet has unit Lebesgue density in a genuine repaired chart, its actual reduced
image has unit density in the transported descended chart.  This closes the quotient-measure part
of the determinant-one branch. -/
theorem normalizedArea_unitLebesgue_on_descendedRefinedImage
    {H : Type uH} {Y : Type uY}
    [Group H] [Fintype H] [MulAction H Y]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y]
    [MeasurableSpace Y] [BorelSpace Y]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H Y]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := Y))
    (hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) S) :
    letI : MulAction H S.Regular :=
      RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
    ∀ (A : _root_.McMullen313Strict.TranslationAtlasGeometry.TranslationAtlas (X := S.Regular))
    (htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) A)
    (μ : Measure Y) [SMulInvariantMeasure H Y μ]
    (c : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular ℂ)
    (eQ : OpenPartialHomeomorph S.Regular (RegularOrbitQ (H := H) S hreg))
    (_heQ : ∀ z, z ∈ eQ.source →
      eQ z = quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)
    (y : S.Regular) (_hyc : y ∈ c.source) (_hye : y ∈ eQ.source)
    (_hunit : UnitLebesgueMassOn (restrictedArea S μ) c
      (descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y)),
    let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg
    let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular)
    let U := descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y
    let φ := fun z : S.Regular => hcan (q z)
    let χQ := QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart (H := H) c eQ
    let χR := TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart hcan χQ
    UnitLebesgueMassOn
      (normalizedCanonicalRegularQuotientArea (H := H) S hreg A htrans μ)
      χR (φ '' U) := by
  dsimp only
  let : MulAction H S.Regular := RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) S hreg
  intro A htrans μ _inst3 c eQ heQ y hyc hye hunit

  try dsimp
  let U := descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y
  let φ := fun z : S.Regular =>
    (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg)
      (quotientMap (H := H) (Y := S.Regular) z)
  let χQ := QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart (H := H) c eQ
  let χR := TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart
    (regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) S hreg) χQ
  have hUopen : IsOpen U :=
    (descendedChartRefinedSheet_open_mem
      (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ y hyc hye).1
  have hU : MeasurableSet U := hUopen.measurableSet
  have hφ : Measurable φ := canonicalReducedParam_measurable (H := H) S hreg
  have hmeasure :
      (normalizedCanonicalRegularQuotientArea
        (H := H) S hreg A htrans μ).restrict (φ '' U) =
        Measure.map φ ((restrictedArea S μ).restrict U) := by
    simpa [U, φ] using
      (normalizedArea_restrict_descendedChartRefinedImage_eq
        (H := H) S hreg A htrans μ c eQ y hyc hye)
  have hcoord : ∀ z ∈ U, χR (φ z) = c z := by
    simpa [U, φ, χQ, χR] using
      (transportedCustomChart_eq_upstairs_on_refinedSheet
        (H := H) S hreg A htrans c eQ heQ y)
  exact unitLebesgueMassOn_of_oneSheet_pushforward
    (restrictedArea S μ)
    (normalizedCanonicalRegularQuotientArea (H := H) S hreg A htrans μ)
    c χR U hU φ hφ hmeasure hunit hcoord

/-- **Advance 6.** A pointwise translation relation between two charts identifies the image of any
subset with an actual translated set in `ℂ`.  The addition order is normalized using commutativity
so that Section 238's `translateSet` applies literally. -/
theorem chart_image_eq_translateSet_of_translation
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X]
    (χ ψ : OpenPartialHomeomorph X ℂ)
    (Ω A : Set X) (t : ℂ)
    (hAΩ : A ⊆ Ω)
    (htrans : ∀ z ∈ Ω, ψ z = χ z + t) :
    ψ '' A = translateSet t (χ '' A) := by
  ext w
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨z, hzA, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨χ z, ⟨z, hzA, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    simpa [translateSet, add_comm] using (htrans z (hAΩ hzA)).symm
  · rintro ⟨v, ⟨z, hzA, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨z, hzA, ?_⟩
    simpa [translateSet, add_comm] using htrans z (hAΩ hzA)

/-- **Advance 7.** Unit Lebesgue density is invariant under a local translation change of chart.
This is the exact bridge from the descended repaired chart to the preferred reduced chart and uses
only translation invariance of planar Lebesgue measure. -/
theorem unitLebesgueMassOn_translation_transfer
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    (μ : Measure X)
    (χ ψ : OpenPartialHomeomorph X ℂ)
    (V Ω : Set X) (t : ℂ)
    (hunit : UnitLebesgueMassOn μ χ V)
    (hΩV : Ω ⊆ V)
    (htrans : ∀ z ∈ Ω, ψ z = χ z + t) :
    UnitLebesgueMassOn μ ψ Ω := by
  intro A hA hAΩ
  have hmass : μ A = (volume : Measure ℂ) (χ '' A) :=
    hunit A hA (Set.Subset.trans hAΩ hΩV)
  have himage : ψ '' A = translateSet t (χ '' A) :=
    chart_image_eq_translateSet_of_translation χ ψ Ω A t hAΩ htrans
  have hvol : (volume : Measure ℂ) (ψ '' A) =
      (volume : Measure ℂ) (χ '' A) :=
    volume_eq_of_eq_translateSet himage
  exact hmass.trans hvol.symm

/-- **Advance 8.** Every point of the actual repaired reduced surface lies in an *open descended
repaired chart region* carrying unit Lebesgue density for the normalized reduced area.  This is the
first completely concrete downstairs unit-density statement: chart, neighbourhood, compatibility,
and measure are all those of the bounded polygon construction. -/
theorem exists_descended_unitLebesgue_neighborhood
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ))
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (x : (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).Regular) :
    let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    let μred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    ∃ χ : OpenPartialHomeomorph Sred.Regular ℂ,
      ∃ W : Set Sred.Regular,
        IsOpen W ∧ x ∈ W ∧ W ⊆ χ.source ∧
        TranslationAtlasCompatibleReplacement.IsTranslationChartFor Sred.atlas χ ∧
        UnitLebesgueMassOn μred χ W := by
  dsimp
  let Sfull := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.surface
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let hreg : _root_.McMullen313Strict.RegularActionToAmbientFreeness.PreservesRegular (H := H) Sfull :=
    boundedPreservesRegular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let : MulAction H Sfull.Regular :=
    RegularOrbitQuotientIdentification.regularMulAction (H := H) Sfull hreg
  let htrans : _root_.McMullen313Strict.NaturalTranslationActionFreeness.IsLocalTranslationAction (H := H) Sfull.atlas := by
    let : MulAction H Sfull.Regular := regularMulAction (H := H) Sfull hreg
    intro h
    exact boundedLocalTranslationOnRegular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly h
  let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let μred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  rcases exists_descended_bounded_chart_at_reduced
      (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly x with
    ⟨a, eQ, hyc, hye, heQ, hxχ, hχ⟩
  let y : Sfull.Regular := canonicalRegularLift (H := H) Sfull hreg x
  let c := BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.regularChart
    (G := G) (H := H) D V CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 a
  let hcan := regularOrbitHomeomorph (H := H) Sfull hreg
  let q := quotientMap (H := H) (Y := Sfull.Regular)
  let χQ := QuotientCompatibleUpstairsChart.customQuotientChart (H := H) c eQ
  let χR := TranslationChartHomeomorphTransport.transportChart hcan χQ
  let U := descendedChartRefinedSheet (H := H) Sfull hreg Sfull.atlas htrans c eQ y
  let φ := fun z : Sfull.Regular => hcan (q z)
  let W := φ '' U
  have hUopen : IsOpen U :=
    (descendedChartRefinedSheet_open_mem
      (H := H) Sfull hreg Sfull.atlas htrans c eQ y hyc hye).1
  have hUsrc : U ⊆ c.source :=
    (descendedChartRefinedSheet_source_subsets
      (H := H) Sfull hreg Sfull.atlas htrans c eQ y).1
  have hup : UnitLebesgueMassOn
      (restrictedArea Sfull (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D)) c U :=
    (boundedRegularChart_unitLebesgue_on_openSubset
      (G := G) H P₀ D V CI CE hreflect hdev
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly a U hUopen hUsrc).2
  let : SMulInvariantMeasure H (Full (H := H) D) (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D) :=
    ConcreteRedundancyAreaInvariance.fullArea_smulInvariantMeasure (G := G) H P₀ D V R hdev
  have hdown : UnitLebesgueMassOn
      (normalizedCanonicalRegularQuotientArea
        (H := H) Sfull hreg Sfull.atlas htrans
          (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D)) χR W := by
    convert! (normalizedArea_unitLebesgue_on_descendedRefinedImage
      (H := H) Sfull hreg Sfull.atlas htrans
      (fullArea (G := G) H P₀ D) c eQ heQ y hyc hye hup) using 1
  have hWopen : IsOpen W := by
    simpa [W, φ, U, hcan, q] using
      (descendedRefinedImage_open
        (H := H) Sfull hreg Sfull.atlas htrans c eQ y hyc hye)
  have hxW : x ∈ W := by
    have hcenter := canonicalReducedParam_mem_descendedRefinedImage
      (H := H) Sfull hreg Sfull.atlas htrans c eQ y hyc hye
    have hxy : hcan (q y) = x := by
      simpa [y, hcan, q] using canonicalRegularLift_maps_to (H := H) Sfull hreg x
    exact ⟨y, (descendedChartRefinedSheet_open_mem
      (H := H) Sfull hreg Sfull.atlas htrans c eQ y hyc hye).2, hxy⟩
  have hWsrc : W ⊆ χR.source := by
    convert! (transportedCustomChart_contains_refined_image
      (H := H) Sfull hreg Sfull.atlas htrans c eQ heQ y) using 1
  refine ⟨χR, W, hWopen, hxW, hWsrc, ?_, ?_⟩
  · dsimp only [Sred, BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface]
    convert! hχ using 1
  · dsimp only [μred, NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea,
      BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface]
    convert! hdown using 1

/-- **Advance 9.** Intersecting the descended unit-density neighbourhood with the translation
comparison neighbourhood transfers unit density to the preferred chart at the chosen reduced point.
Thus every point has an open preferred-chart neighbourhood on which normalized area is exactly
planar Lebesgue measure in preferred coordinates. -/
theorem exists_preferred_unitLebesgue_neighborhood
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ))
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (x : (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly).Regular) :
    let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    let μred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    ∃ Ω : Set Sred.Regular,
      IsOpen Ω ∧ x ∈ Ω ∧ Ω ⊆ (Sred.atlas.chartAt x).source ∧
      UnitLebesgueMassOn μred (Sred.atlas.chartAt x) Ω := by
  dsimp
  let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let μred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  rcases exists_descended_unitLebesgue_neighborhood
      (G := G) H P₀ D V hdev R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly x with
    ⟨χ, W, hWopen, hxW, hWsrc, hχ, hunitW⟩
  rcases local_translation_compare_of_compatible Sred.atlas χ hχ x
      (hWsrc hxW) with
    ⟨T, hTopen, hxT, hTsub, t, htrans⟩
  let Ω := W ∩ T
  have hΩopen : IsOpen Ω := hWopen.inter hTopen
  have hxΩ : x ∈ Ω := ⟨hxW, hxT⟩
  have hΩW : Ω ⊆ W := Set.inter_subset_left
  have hΩpref : Ω ⊆ (Sred.atlas.chartAt x).source := by
    intro z hz
    exact (hTsub hz.2).2
  have htransΩ : ∀ z ∈ Ω, Sred.atlas.chartAt x z = χ z + t := by
    intro z hz
    exact htrans z hz.2
  have hunitΩ : UnitLebesgueMassOn μred (Sred.atlas.chartAt x) Ω :=
    unitLebesgueMassOn_translation_transfer
      μred χ (Sred.atlas.chartAt x) W Ω t hunitW hΩW htransΩ
  exact ⟨Ω, hΩopen, hxΩ, hΩpref, hunitΩ⟩

/-- Pointwise preferred-chart unit density: every point has an open neighbourhood inside its
preferred translation chart on which the measure is exactly planar Lebesgue measure setwise. -/
def LocallyUnitLebesguePreferred
    {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := X))
    (μ : Measure S.Regular) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : S.Regular, ∃ U : Set S.Regular,
    IsOpen U ∧ x ∈ U ∧ U ⊆ (S.atlas.chartAt x).source ∧
    UnitLebesgueMassOn μ (S.atlas.chartAt x) U

/-- **Advance 10.** The actual normalized reduced area of the repaired bounded polygon surface is
pointwise unit Lebesgue measure in the preferred reduced translation charts.  Therefore every
quotient, multiplicity, repaired-chart, and translation-overlap issue in the determinant-one area
branch is now closed.  What remains is solely to combine this local density with the already-proved
real-affine local normal form of an arbitrary affine automorphism. -/
theorem normalizedBoundedReducedArea_locallyUnitLebesguePreferred
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ))
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite) :
    LocallyUnitLebesguePreferred
      (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
      (_root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly) := by
  intro x
  exact exists_preferred_unitLebesgue_neighborhood
    (G := G) H P₀ D V hdev R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly x

end ReducedPreferredUnitDensityClosure


/-! ## 298. Updated boundary after closing normalized reduced local unit density

The normalized reduced area is now proved to be locally ordinary planar Lebesgue measure in the
*preferred* reduced translation chart at every regular point.  The proof uses the exact normalized
one-sheet restriction identity, the repaired full-chart unit-density law on the same refined sheet,
and the coordinate commutative square from Section 291.  The descended image is open and contains
the chosen reduced point.  Compatibility then supplies a translation overlap with the preferred
chart, and translation invariance of planar Lebesgue measure transfers the setwise density without
any new scalar.

Thus the determinant-one area branch no longer has any quotient, multiplicity, second-countability,
chart-choice, restriction, interior/edge, normalization, or local-density gap.  The sole remaining
measure step is the affine one: intersect the preferred unit-density neighbourhoods around `x` and
`F⁻¹ x` with the local affine-normal-form neighbourhood of `F.symm`, identify the target coordinate
map with `z ↦ c + L⁻¹ z`, invoke the general real-affine restricted Jacobian theorem of Section 283,
and convert the resulting setwise equality into the `LocallyRestrictionEqual` statement required by
`PointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea`.  The second-countable globalization theorem of Section 285 then
immediately gives `ScalesFlatArea`.
-/

/-! ## 299. Final affine assembly for the normalized reduced flat area

Section 298 closed the geometric and quotient-theoretic part of the area argument: the normalized
reduced measure is locally unit Lebesgue measure in the preferred translation chart at every regular
point.  We now perform the final affine change-of-variables assembly without ever treating a partial
chart as a globally measurable map.  First we restrict an `OpenPartialHomeomorph` to an honest
homeomorphism between its source and target subtypes; this gives the missing Borel-image statement
for measurable subsets of a chart source.  We then combine local unit density, the affine normal
form of `F.symm`, and Section 283's arbitrary real-affine Jacobian formula. -/

namespace PreferredAffineScalingClosure

open MeasureTheory
open TranslationAtlasGeometry
open TranslationAffineAutomorphisms
open VeechAffineDerivative
open AffineFlatAreaScaling
open GeneralComplexRealAffineJacobian
open PointwiseLocalScalingAssembly
open RepairedRegularChartUnitDensity
open ReducedPreferredUnitDensityClosure
open RepairedSecondCountabilityClosure
open NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure
open FullCopyUnfolding
open FullCopyUnfoldingTopology
open FullRegularFlatChartRestriction
open BoundedRegularAtlasRepair
open BoundedFullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction
open BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation
open ReducedQuotientTopology

universe uX uG uE uI uJ

/-- **Advance 1.** Setwise unit Lebesgue density is monotone under restriction of the region.  This
lets us intersect the source/target density neighbourhoods with an affine-normal-form neighbourhood
without repeating any area calculation. -/
theorem unitLebesgueMassOn_mono
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    {μ : Measure X} {χ : OpenPartialHomeomorph X ℂ} {U V : Set X}
    (hU : UnitLebesgueMassOn μ χ U) (hVU : V ⊆ U) :
    UnitLebesgueMassOn μ χ V := by
  intro A hA hAV
  exact hU A hA (Set.Subset.trans hAV hVU)

/-- **Advance 2.** An open partial homeomorphism is an honest homeomorphism after restricting domain
and codomain to its source and target subtypes.  This is the safe measurable object attached to a
preferred translation chart. -/
noncomputable def chartSourceTargetHomeomorph
    {X Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Y]
    (χ : OpenPartialHomeomorph X Y) : χ.source ≃ₜ χ.target where
  toEquiv := χ.toPartialEquiv.toEquiv
  continuous_toFun := by
    exact χ.continuousOn.mapsToRestrict χ.mapsTo
  continuous_invFun := by
    exact (χ.symm).continuousOn.mapsToRestrict (χ.symm).mapsTo

/-- **Advance 3.** A measurable subset of the source of a preferred chart has measurable coordinate
image.  Crucially, this uses the source-target homeomorphism from Advance 2 and therefore makes no
claim that the ambient partial-chart function is measurable outside its source. -/
theorem measurableSet_chart_image
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X] [BorelSpace X]
    (χ : OpenPartialHomeomorph X ℂ)
    {A : Set X} (hA : MeasurableSet A) (hAsrc : A ⊆ χ.source) :
    MeasurableSet (χ '' A) := by
  let e := chartSourceTargetHomeomorph χ
  let As : Set χ.source := Subtype.val ⁻¹' A
  have hAs : MeasurableSet As := hA.preimage measurable_subtype_coe
  have hEAs : MeasurableSet (e '' As) :=
    e.toMeasurableEquiv.measurableSet_image.mpr hAs
  have hval : MeasurableSet (Subtype.val '' (e '' As)) :=
    χ.open_target.measurableSet.subtype_image hEAs
  have heq : Subtype.val '' (e '' As) = χ '' A := by
    ext y
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨z, ⟨x, hxA, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨x.1, ?_, ?_⟩
      · exact hxA
      · rfl
    · rintro ⟨x, hxA, rfl⟩
      have hxsrc : x ∈ χ.source := hAsrc hxA
      let sx : χ.source := ⟨x, hxsrc⟩
      let z : χ.target := e sx
      refine ⟨z, ?_, ?_⟩
      · refine ⟨sx, ?_, rfl⟩
        exact hxA
      · rfl
  rw [heq] at hval
  exact hval

/-- **Advance 4.** Section 283's restricted affine Jacobian identity can be evaluated on the whole
plane to obtain the exact setwise relation needed below: the source-coordinate mass equals
`jacobianScale L` times the mass of its image under the affine map with linear part `L⁻¹`. -/
theorem volume_eq_jacobianScale_mul_affineInv_image
    (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ)
    {T : Set ℂ} (hT : MeasurableSet T) :
    (volume : Measure ℂ) T =
      jacobianScale L *
        (volume : Measure ℂ) (planeAffineMap (inv L) c '' T) := by
  have h := congrArg (fun ν : Measure ℂ => ν Set.univ)
    (map_planeAffineMap_inv_restrict_smul_volume
      (1 : ENNReal) L c hT)
  rw [Measure.map_apply
    (measurable_planeAffineMap (inv L) c) MeasurableSet.univ] at h
  simpa only [Set.preimage_univ, Measure.restrict_apply MeasurableSet.univ,
    Set.univ_inter, one_smul, Measure.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul] using h

/-- **Advance 5.** The local affine normal form transports coordinate images exactly.  For any
subset of the image of a source neighbourhood, its target-chart image is the real-affine image of
the source-chart image of its homeomorphic preimage. -/
theorem chart_image_eq_affine_image_preimage
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X]
    (f : Homeomorph X X)
    (χs χt : OpenPartialHomeomorph X ℂ)
    (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ)
    {V A : Set X}
    (hform : ∀ z : X, z ∈ V →
      χt (f z) = planeAffineMap (inv L) c (χs z))
    (hAV : A ⊆ f '' V) :
    χt '' A =
      planeAffineMap (inv L) c '' (χs '' (f ⁻¹' A)) := by
  have hpreV : f ⁻¹' A ⊆ V := by
    intro z hz
    rcases hAV hz with ⟨v, hvV, hvz⟩
    have hv_eq_z : v = z := f.injective hvz
    simpa [hv_eq_z] using hvV
  ext w
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨a, haA, rfl⟩
    let z : X := f.symm a
    have hzA : z ∈ f ⁻¹' A := by
      change f z ∈ A
      simpa [z] using haA
    have hzV : z ∈ V := hpreV hzA
    refine ⟨χs z, ⟨z, hzA, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    simpa [z] using (hform z hzV).symm
  · rintro ⟨u, ⟨z, hzA, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    have hzV : z ∈ V := hpreV hzA
    refine ⟨f z, hzA, ?_⟩
    exact hform z hzV

/-- **Advance 6.** Local affine change of variables at the setwise level.  If the same measure has
unit Lebesgue density in a source preferred chart on `V` and in the target preferred chart on
`f '' V`, and the coordinate expression of `f` has derivative `L⁻¹`, then the pushforward mass of
every measurable subset of `f '' V` is exactly `jacobianScale L` times its original mass. -/
theorem map_homeomorph_apply_eq_jacobian_mul
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X] [BorelSpace X]
    (μ : Measure X) (f : Homeomorph X X)
    (χs χt : OpenPartialHomeomorph X ℂ)
    (L : PlaneRealLinearEquiv) (c : ℂ)
    {V : Set X}
    (hVsrc : V ⊆ χs.source)
    (hunitS : UnitLebesgueMassOn μ χs V)
    (hunitT : UnitLebesgueMassOn μ χt (f '' V))
    (hform : ∀ z : X, z ∈ V →
      χt (f z) = planeAffineMap (inv L) c (χs z))
    {A : Set X} (hA : MeasurableSet A) (hAimg : A ⊆ f '' V) :
    Measure.map f μ A = jacobianScale L * μ A := by
  have hpre : MeasurableSet (f ⁻¹' A) := hA.preimage f.measurable
  have hpreV : f ⁻¹' A ⊆ V := by
    intro z hz
    rcases hAimg hz with ⟨v, hvV, hvz⟩
    have hv_eq_z : v = z := f.injective hvz
    simpa [hv_eq_z] using hvV
  have hpreSrc : f ⁻¹' A ⊆ χs.source :=
    Set.Subset.trans hpreV hVsrc
  have hcoord : MeasurableSet (χs '' (f ⁻¹' A)) :=
    measurableSet_chart_image χs hpre hpreSrc
  have himage := chart_image_eq_affine_image_preimage
    f χs χt L c hform hAimg
  calc
    Measure.map f μ A = μ (f ⁻¹' A) := by
      rw [Measure.map_apply f.measurable hA]
    _ = (volume : Measure ℂ) (χs '' (f ⁻¹' A)) :=
      hunitS (f ⁻¹' A) hpre hpreV
    _ = jacobianScale L *
        (volume : Measure ℂ)
          (planeAffineMap (inv L) c '' (χs '' (f ⁻¹' A))) :=
      volume_eq_jacobianScale_mul_affineInv_image L c hcoord
    _ = jacobianScale L * (volume : Measure ℂ) (χt '' A) := by
      rw [← himage]
    _ = jacobianScale L * μ A := by
      rw [hunitT A hA hAimg]

/-- **Advance 7.** Equality on all measurable subsets of a measurable region packages into equality
of restricted measures.  This is the exact bridge from Advance 6's safe setwise argument to the
`LocallyRestrictionEqual` interface of Section 285. -/
theorem restrict_eq_of_eq_on_measurable_subsets
    {X : Type uX} [MeasurableSpace X]
    {ν ρ : Measure X} {W : Set X}
    (hW : MeasurableSet W)
    (h : ∀ A : Set X, MeasurableSet A → A ⊆ W → ν A = ρ A) :
    ν.restrict W = ρ.restrict W := by
  apply Measure.ext
  intro A hA
  rw [Measure.restrict_apply hA, Measure.restrict_apply hA]
  exact h (A ∩ W) (hA.inter hW) Set.inter_subset_right

/-- **Advance 8.** Abstract final affine assembly.  Any translation surface whose measure is locally
unit Lebesgue in its preferred charts automatically satisfies the pointwise local flat-area scaling
law for every affine automorphism.  The proof intersects source density, target density, and the
`F.symm` affine-normal-form neighbourhood and invokes Advances 3--7. -/
theorem pointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea_of_locallyUnitLebesguePreferred
    {X : Type uX} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X]
    (S : RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.RegularTranslationSurface (X := X))
    [BorelSpace S.Regular]
    (μ : Measure S.Regular)
    (hunit : LocallyUnitLebesguePreferred S μ) :
    PointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea S μ := by
  intro F x
  let f : Homeomorph S.Regular S.Regular := F.toHomeomorph.symm
  let y : S.Regular := F.toHomeomorph x
  have hfy : f y = x := by
    simp [f, y]
  rcases hunit y with ⟨Us, hUsOpen, hyUs, hUsSrc, hunitUs⟩
  rcases hunit x with ⟨Ut, hUtOpen, hxUt, hUtSrc, hunitUt⟩
  rcases F.locally_affine_symm y with
    ⟨Ua, hUaOpen, hyUa, hUaSrc, _hmapUa, c, hformUa⟩
  let V : Set S.Regular := Ua ∩ Us ∩ f ⁻¹' Ut
  have hVOpen : IsOpen V :=
    (hUaOpen.inter hUsOpen).inter (hUtOpen.preimage f.continuous)
  have hyV : y ∈ V := by
    refine ⟨⟨hyUa, hyUs⟩, ?_⟩
    simpa [hfy] using hxUt
  have hVUs : V ⊆ Us := by
    intro z hz
    exact hz.1.2
  have hVUa : V ⊆ Ua := by
    intro z hz
    exact hz.1.1
  have hVsrc : V ⊆ (S.atlas.chartAt y).source :=
    Set.Subset.trans hVUa hUaSrc
  have hfVUt : f '' V ⊆ Ut := by
    rintro z ⟨w, hwV, rfl⟩
    exact hwV.2
  have hfVsrc : f '' V ⊆ (S.atlas.chartAt x).source :=
    Set.Subset.trans hfVUt hUtSrc
  have hfVOpen : IsOpen (f '' V) := f.isOpenMap V hVOpen
  have hx_fV : x ∈ f '' V := by
    refine ⟨y, hyV, ?_⟩
    exact hfy
  have hunitS : UnitLebesgueMassOn μ (S.atlas.chartAt y) V :=
    unitLebesgueMassOn_mono hunitUs hVUs
  have hunitT : UnitLebesgueMassOn μ (S.atlas.chartAt x) (f '' V) :=
    unitLebesgueMassOn_mono hunitUt hfVUt
  have hform : ∀ z : S.Regular, z ∈ V →
      S.atlas.chartAt x (f z) =
        planeAffineMap (inv F.derivative) c (S.atlas.chartAt y z) := by
    intro z hz
    have hzUa : z ∈ Ua := hVUa hz
    simpa only [← hfy, planeAffineMap, add_comm] using hformUa z hzUa
  have hset : ∀ A : Set S.Regular, MeasurableSet A → A ⊆ f '' V →
      Measure.map f μ A = (jacobianScale F.derivative • μ) A := by
    intro A hA hAimg
    have hmass := map_homeomorph_apply_eq_jacobian_mul
      μ f (S.atlas.chartAt y) (S.atlas.chartAt x)
      F.derivative c hVsrc hunitS hunitT hform hA hAimg
    simpa only [Measure.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul] using hmass
  refine ⟨f '' V, hfVOpen, hx_fV, ?_⟩
  have hrest := restrict_eq_of_eq_on_measurable_subsets
    hfVOpen.measurableSet hset
  simpa [f] using hrest

/-- **Advance 9.** The actual normalized reduced area of the repaired bounded polygon surface now
satisfies both the pointwise-local and global affine Jacobian scaling laws.  This closes the entire
`ScalesFlatArea` half of the determinant-one argument. -/
theorem normalizedBoundedReducedArea_pointwise_and_scales
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ))
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite) :
    let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    let μred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
      g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    PointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea Sred μred ∧ ScalesFlatArea Sred μred := by
  dsimp
  let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let μred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  have hunit : LocallyUnitLebesguePreferred Sred μred := by
    simpa [Sred, μred] using
      normalizedBoundedReducedArea_locallyUnitLebesguePreferred
        (G := G) H P₀ D V hdev R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  have hpoint : PointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea Sred μred :=
    pointwiseLocallyScalesFlatArea_of_locallyUnitLebesguePreferred Sred μred hunit
  have hscale : ScalesFlatArea Sred μred := by
    exact normalizedBoundedReducedArea_scales_of_pointwise
      (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly hpoint
  exact ⟨hpoint, hscale⟩

/-- **Advance 10.** Combining Advance 9 with Section 281's finite/nonzero theorem produces the
actual `HasFiniteFlatAreaScaling` package for the repaired bounded reduced polygon surface.  Thus the
finite-area determinant-one mechanism of Sections 207--208 is now available with no geometric or
measure-theoretic hypothesis left unproved inside this branch. -/
theorem boundedReduced_hasFiniteFlatAreaScaling
    {G : Type uG} [Group G] [Fintype G]
    (H : Subgroup G)
    {E : Type uE}
    (P₀ : CompactPlanarPolygonArea.Carrier)
    [MulAction H P₀.carrier] [MulAction H E]
    (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P₀.carrier E)
    [TopologicalSpace G] [DiscreteTopology G]
    [ContinuousConstSMul H P₀.carrier]
    [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)
    (hdev : V.dev = fun p : P₀.carrier => (p : ℂ))
    (R : PlanarRedundancyDevelopingData.Data (H := H) D V)
    {I : Type uI} {J : Type uJ}
    (CI : FullInteriorFlatCharts.InteriorCover (H := H) D V I)
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (hreflect : ∀ e : E, D.reflect e ≠ 1)
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (H := H) (G := G) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P₀.carrier) D)]
    [Finite H]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P₀.carrier) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite) :
    HasFiniteFlatAreaScaling
      (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
        g0 p0 hp0 hpoly) := by
  let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  let μred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.NormalizedFiniteAreaClosure.normalizedBoundedReducedArea (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect
    g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  have hpair := normalizedBoundedReducedArea_pointwise_and_scales
    (G := G) H P₀ D V hdev R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  have hfinite : IsFiniteNonzeroFlatArea Sred μred := by
    simpa [Sred, μred] using
      normalizedBoundedReducedArea_finite_nonzero
        (G := G) H P₀ D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
  refine ⟨μred, hfinite, ?_⟩
  try simpa [Sred, μred] using hpair.2

end PreferredAffineScalingClosure


/-! ## 300. Updated boundary after closing the normalized finite-area scaling branch

The normalized reduced area branch is now formally closed at the theorem-interface level.  Local
unit Lebesgue density in preferred charts has been combined with the local affine normal form of an
arbitrary affine automorphism and the full real-affine Jacobian theorem.  The only subtle measurable
step -- Borel measurability of the image of a measurable subset under a partial chart -- is handled
by restricting the chart to a genuine homeomorphism between its source and target subtypes; no
global measurability of a partial chart is assumed.

Consequently the concrete repaired bounded reduced polygon surface now carries one and the same
normalized measure which is finite, nonzero, and satisfies the global affine Jacobian scaling law.
In particular `HasFiniteFlatAreaScaling` is available directly, so every orientation-preserving
affine derivative has determinant one via the already-proved abstract finite-measure rigidity
machinery.

This closes the determinant-one / normalized-flat-area branch itself.  The remaining work toward a
final theorem named `mcMullen_3_13` is no longer measure-theoretic: the next audit must return to the
dynamical implication connecting nonminimal directions, complete periodicity, and the precise
reduced/unreduced lattice-surface dichotomy used by McMullen's question.
-/

/-! ## 301. Reattaching the edge reflection to the repaired bounded full/reduced surfaces

Section 300 closed the normalized finite-area scaling branch on the non-vacuous bounded surface.
The next audit exposes a separate historical dependency in the dynamical branch: the polygon-edge
reflection theorems of Sections 168--190 were instantiated with the obsolete whole-half-plane
`FlatEdgeCover`, whereas Sections 261--300 replaced that cover by `BoundedFlatEdgeCover` and rebuilt
the actual compact-polygon-compatible full and reduced surfaces.

The quotient algebra of the reflection never depended on the obsolete chart domain: left
multiplication preserves the intrinsic combinatorial regular locus, commutes with redundancy, and
therefore descends through the same effective finite orbit quotient.  We now reattach those facts to
the repaired bounded surfaces and identify the transported intrinsic reflection with the ambient
`edgeSigma` on the actual reduced unfolding.  This section deliberately stops before local
star-affinity; its purpose is to remove the old surface from the *global self-map* layer so that the
next section can port only the genuinely chart-dependent mirror argument. -/

