/-- **Advance 9.** The actual edge reflection restricted to the repaired reduced regular locus is
continuous.  This closes the topological self-map part of the fixed-mirror input on the correct
surface. -/
theorem restrictedEdgeSigma_bounded_continuous
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D)]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (e : E) :
    let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    let hregR := edgeSigma_preserves_boundedReduced_regular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly e
    Continuous ((RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.restrictMap Sred)
      (edgeSigma (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D e) hregR) := by
  dsimp
  exact RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.continuous_restrictMap
    (_root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly)
    (edgeSigma (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D e)
    (edgeSigma_preserves_boundedReduced_regular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly e)
    (FullCopyUnfoldingTopologicalActions.edgeSigma_continuous
      (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D e)

/-- **Advance 10.** The same repaired reduced restriction is an involution.  Thus continuity,
regular-locus preservation, quotient identification, and involutivity of the actual edge reflection
are all now established on the non-vacuous bounded surface; only its chartwise anti-affine/fixed
mirror geometry remains to be migrated. -/
theorem restrictedEdgeSigma_bounded_involutive
    [T2Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Full (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D)]
    [T1Space (_root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D)]
    (g0 : G) (p0 : P) (hp0 : _root_.McMullen313Strict.CombinatorialFullRegularLocus.AtMostOneEdgeAt (H := H) D p0)
    (hpoly : (FullRegularTranslationAtlasConstruction.polygonSingularSet
      (H := H) D).Finite)
    (e : E) :
    let Sred := _root_.McMullen313Strict.BoundedRedundancyLocalTranslation.boundedReducedSurface
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly
    let hregR := edgeSigma_preserves_boundedReduced_regular
      (G := G) (H := H) D V R CI CE hreflect g0 p0 hp0 hpoly e
    Function.Involutive ((RegularTranslationSurfaceGeometry.restrictMap Sred)
      (edgeSigma (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D e) hregR) := by
  dsimp
  intro z
  apply Subtype.ext
  exact FullCopyUnfolding.edgeSigma_involutive
    (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D e
      (z : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.Reduced (G := G) (H := H) (P := P) D)

end BoundedEdgeReflectionReattachment


/-! ## 302. Updated dynamical boundary after removing the old surface from the reflection map

The audit after Section 300 found a concrete mismatch which is more fundamental than the still-open
leafwise Veech theorem: Sections 168--190 attached the edge-reflection dynamics to the historical
full/reduced surface built from `FlatEdgeCover`, while Section 229 proves that this whole-half-plane
edge datum has no literal compact-polygon inclusion instance.  The area branch had already migrated
to `BoundedFlatEdgeCover`, but the dynamical branch had not.

Section 301 repairs the atlas-independent half of that mismatch.  On the repaired bounded full
surface every left action preserves the same intrinsic regular set and the selected edge reflection
is a continuous involution.  The effective quotient reflection is transported through the canonical
regular-orbit homeomorphism, proved to coincide pointwise with the ambient `edgeSigma`, and hence
`edgeSigma` is now a continuous involution on the regular locus of the actual repaired
`boundedReducedSurface`.

The remaining geometric migration is sharply localized: prove local star-affinity and construct a
regular fixed mirror for this bounded restriction.  The bounded topological edge chart already has
literal conjugation normal form (`edgeAction_boundedFullEdgeChart_conj`), while the repaired physical
charts already cover the whole full regular locus.  What must still be ported from Sections 176--187
is the one-edge global normalization and the finite star-difference argument for the bounded chart
family.  Only after that migration is complete is it legitimate to invoke the leafwise Veech layer
for the compact-polygon surface used in McMullen's question.
-/

/-! ## 303. A bounded edge window still determines the global real-linear reflection law

Section 302 isolated the precise remaining migration problem.  The historical global
`FlatLocalEdgeParam` extracted the linear reflection law by evaluating at the three universal
half-plane points `0,1,i`; that argument cannot be reused literally for a compact polygon because a
correct edge chart is only defined on a bounded relatively-open window.  The global conclusion,
however, is genuinely local.  If one point of the bounded window lies on the boundary, relative
openness supplies a small horizontal displacement and a small positive-imaginary displacement still
inside the window.  Subtracting the two flat formulas at those nearby points determines the action
on two independent real directions.  Real-linearity then gives the same global conjugation law on
all of `ℂ`.

This section makes that replacement explicit.  It is the exact bounded-window analogue of Section
176 and uses no point outside the actual compact-polygon chart. -/

namespace BoundedEdgeReflectionScaleIntertwining

open BoundedEdgeWindowRepair
open BoundedRegularAtlasRepair
open FullCopyUnfolding
open EuclideanEdgeTranslation
open PlanarDevelopedEdgeData

universe uG uP uE uJ

variable {G : Type uG} [Group G]
variable (H : Subgroup G)
variable {P : Type uP} {E : Type uE}
variable [TopologicalSpace P]
variable [MulAction H P] [MulAction H E]
variable (D : _root_.McMullen313Strict.FullCopyUnfolding.EdgeGluingData (G := G) H P E)
variable [DistribMulAction G ℂ] [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
variable (V : PlanarDevelopedEdgeData.Data (H := H) D)

/-- **Advance 1.** A point of a bounded half-plane window has a genuine metric ball in the
relative upper-half-plane topology which stays inside the window.  At a boundary point this ball is
a half-disk, which is exactly what the repaired reflection argument needs. -/
theorem exists_window_radius
    (W : HalfPlaneWindow) (z0 : W.Point) :
    ∃ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε ∧ Metric.ball z0.1 ε ⊆ W.carrier := by
  rcases (Metric.isOpen_iff.mp W.isOpen_carrier) z0.1 z0.2 with
    ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩
  exact ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩

/-- **Advance 2.** At a boundary point of a relatively open upper-half-plane window one can move a
nonzero real amount horizontally and remain in the same window. -/
theorem exists_horizontal_window_point
    (W : HalfPlaneWindow) (z0 : W.Point)
    (hboundary : ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ).im = 0) :
    ∃ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ ∧ ∃ zR : W.Point,
      ((zR.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) =
        ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) + (δ : ℂ) := by
  rcases exists_window_radius W z0 with ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩
  let δ : ℝ := ε / 2
  have hδ : 0 < δ := by dsimp [δ]; linarith
  let u : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane :=
    ⟨((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) + (δ : ℂ), by
      
      simp [hboundary]⟩
  have huBall : u ∈ Metric.ball z0.1 ε := by
    rw [Metric.mem_ball]
    change dist (((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) + (δ : ℂ))
      ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) < ε
    rw [dist_eq_norm]
    simp [δ, abs_of_pos hε]
    linarith
  have hu : u ∈ W.carrier := hball huBall
  refine ⟨δ, hδ, ⟨u, hu⟩, ?_⟩
  rfl

/-- **Advance 3.** The same relative openness supplies an independent positive-imaginary
perturbation.  Thus a genuine bounded edge window still contains two infinitesimal real directions
at each boundary point. -/
theorem exists_vertical_window_point
    (W : HalfPlaneWindow) (z0 : W.Point)
    (hboundary : ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ).im = 0) :
    ∃ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ ∧ ∃ zI : W.Point,
      ((zI.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) =
        ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) + (δ : ℂ) * Complex.I := by
  rcases exists_window_radius W z0 with ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩
  let δ : ℝ := ε / 2
  have hδ : 0 < δ := by dsimp [δ]; linarith
  let u : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane :=
    ⟨((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) + (δ : ℂ) * Complex.I, by
      
      simp [hboundary, le_of_lt hδ]⟩
  have huBall : u ∈ Metric.ball z0.1 ε := by
    rw [Metric.mem_ball]
    change dist (((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) + (δ : ℂ) * Complex.I)
      ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) < ε
    rw [dist_eq_norm]
    simp [ δ, abs_of_pos hε]
    linarith
  have hu : u ∈ W.carrier := hball huBall
  refine ⟨δ, hδ, ⟨u, hu⟩, ?_⟩
  rfl

omit [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ] in
/-- **Advance 4.** Subtracting the two bounded flat formulas along the horizontal perturbation
shows that the selected reflection fixes one nonzero multiple of the chart scale.  No universal
point `1` is used. -/
theorem reflect_scaled_horizontal [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    {e : E} {W : HalfPlaneWindow}
    (L : WindowFlatLocalEdgeParam (H := H) D V W (1 : G) e)
    (z0 : W.Point)
    (hboundary : ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ).im = 0) :
    ∃ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ ∧
      D.reflect e • (L.scale * (δ : ℂ)) = L.scale * (δ : ℂ) := by
  rcases exists_horizontal_window_point W z0 hboundary with
    ⟨δ, hδ, zR, hzR⟩
  let zc : ℂ := ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ)
  have hz0star : star zc = zc := by
    apply Complex.ext
    · simp [zc]
    · simp [zc, hboundary]
  have hzRstar : star (((zR.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ)) =
      ((zR.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ) := by
    rw [hzR]
    change star (zc + (δ : ℂ)) = zc + (δ : ℂ)
    rw [star_add, hz0star]
    simp []
  have hf0 : V.dev (L.toP z0) = L.scale * zc + L.offset := by
    simpa [zc] using L.first_flat z0
  have hfR : V.dev (L.toP zR) =
      L.scale * (zc + (δ : ℂ)) + L.offset := by
    simpa [zc, hzR] using L.first_flat zR
  have hs0 : D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP z0) +
      sideTranslationConstant 1 (D.reflect e) (V.edgeBase e) =
        L.scale * zc + L.offset := by
    simpa [zc, hz0star] using L.second_flat z0
  have hsR : D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP zR) +
      sideTranslationConstant 1 (D.reflect e) (V.edgeBase e) =
        L.scale * (zc + (δ : ℂ)) + L.offset := by
    have hs := L.second_flat zR
    rw [hzRstar] at hs
    simpa only [hzR, one_mul, zc] using hs
  have hdev : V.dev (L.toP zR) - V.dev (L.toP z0) =
      L.scale * (δ : ℂ) := by
    linear_combination hfR - hf0
  have hsig : D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP zR) -
      D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP z0) = L.scale * (δ : ℂ) := by
    linear_combination hsR - hs0
  refine ⟨δ, hδ, ?_⟩
  calc
    D.reflect e • (L.scale * (δ : ℂ)) =
        D.reflect e • (V.dev (L.toP zR) - V.dev (L.toP z0)) := by rw [hdev]
    _ = D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP zR) -
        D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP z0) := by rw [smul_sub]
    _ = L.scale * (δ : ℂ) := hsig

omit [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ] in
/-- **Advance 5.** The positive-imaginary perturbation similarly gives an anti-fixed nonzero
multiple of `scale * I`.  This replaces the historical evaluation at the universal point `i`. -/
theorem reflect_scaled_vertical [SMulCommClass G ℝ ℂ]
    {e : E} {W : HalfPlaneWindow}
    (L : WindowFlatLocalEdgeParam (H := H) D V W (1 : G) e)
    (z0 : W.Point)
    (hboundary : ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ).im = 0) :
    ∃ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ ∧
      D.reflect e • (L.scale * ((δ : ℂ) * Complex.I)) =
        -(L.scale * ((δ : ℂ) * Complex.I)) := by
  rcases exists_vertical_window_point W z0 hboundary with
    ⟨δ, hδ, zI, hzI⟩
  let zc : ℂ := ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ)
  have hz0star : star zc = zc := by
    apply Complex.ext
    · simp [zc]
    · simp [zc, hboundary]
  have hzIstar : star (((zI.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ)) =
      zc - (δ : ℂ) * Complex.I := by
    rw [hzI]
    change star (zc + (δ : ℂ) * Complex.I) = _
    rw [star_add, hz0star, star_mul]
    simp [ sub_eq_add_neg, mul_comm]
  have hf0 : V.dev (L.toP z0) = L.scale * zc + L.offset := by
    simpa [zc] using L.first_flat z0
  have hfI : V.dev (L.toP zI) =
      L.scale * (zc + (δ : ℂ) * Complex.I) + L.offset := by
    simpa [zc, hzI] using L.first_flat zI
  have hs0 : D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP z0) +
      sideTranslationConstant 1 (D.reflect e) (V.edgeBase e) =
        L.scale * zc + L.offset := by
    simpa [zc, hz0star] using L.second_flat z0
  have hsI : D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP zI) +
      sideTranslationConstant 1 (D.reflect e) (V.edgeBase e) =
        L.scale * (zc - (δ : ℂ) * Complex.I) + L.offset := by
    simpa only [hzIstar, one_mul, zc] using L.second_flat zI
  have hdev : V.dev (L.toP zI) - V.dev (L.toP z0) =
      L.scale * ((δ : ℂ) * Complex.I) := by
    linear_combination hfI - hf0
  have hsig : D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP zI) -
      D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP z0) =
        -(L.scale * ((δ : ℂ) * Complex.I)) := by
    linear_combination hsI - hs0
  refine ⟨δ, hδ, ?_⟩
  calc
    D.reflect e • (L.scale * ((δ : ℂ) * Complex.I)) =
        D.reflect e • (V.dev (L.toP zI) - V.dev (L.toP z0)) := by rw [hdev]
    _ = D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP zI) -
        D.reflect e • V.dev (L.toP z0) := by rw [smul_sub]
    _ = -(L.scale * ((δ : ℂ) * Complex.I)) := hsig

/-- **Advance 6.** Cancelling the nonzero horizontal displacement recovers the exact fixed scale
vector.  Thus boundedness of the chart has not weakened the first eigendirection. -/
theorem reflect_scale
    {e : E} {W : HalfPlaneWindow}
    (L : WindowFlatLocalEdgeParam (H := H) D V W (1 : G) e)
    (z0 : W.Point)
    (hboundary : ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ).im = 0) :
    D.reflect e • L.scale = L.scale := by
  rcases reflect_scaled_horizontal (H := H) D V L z0 hboundary with
    ⟨δ, hδ, hscaled⟩
  have hδc : (δ : ℂ) ≠ 0 := by
    exact_mod_cast (ne_of_gt hδ)
  have hcomm :
      D.reflect e • (L.scale * (δ : ℂ)) =
        (D.reflect e • L.scale) * (δ : ℂ) := by
    calc
      D.reflect e • (L.scale * (δ : ℂ)) =
          D.reflect e • (δ • L.scale) := by
            simp [Complex.real_smul, mul_comm]
      _ = δ • (D.reflect e • L.scale) :=
        smul_comm (D.reflect e) δ L.scale
      _ = (D.reflect e • L.scale) * (δ : ℂ) := by
        simp [Complex.real_smul, mul_comm]
  have hscaled' : (D.reflect e • L.scale) * (δ : ℂ) =
      L.scale * (δ : ℂ) := by
    rw [← hcomm]
    exact hscaled
  exact mul_right_cancel₀ hδc hscaled'

/-- **Advance 7.** Cancelling the nonzero vertical displacement likewise recovers the exact
anti-fixed vector `scale * I`. -/
theorem reflect_scale_mul_I
    {e : E} {W : HalfPlaneWindow}
    (L : WindowFlatLocalEdgeParam (H := H) D V W (1 : G) e)
    (z0 : W.Point)
    (hboundary : ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ).im = 0) :
    D.reflect e • (L.scale * Complex.I) = -(L.scale * Complex.I) := by
  rcases reflect_scaled_vertical (H := H) D V L z0 hboundary with
    ⟨δ, hδ, hscaled⟩
  have hδc : (δ : ℂ) ≠ 0 := by
    exact_mod_cast (ne_of_gt hδ)
  have hcomm :
      D.reflect e • ((L.scale * Complex.I) * (δ : ℂ)) =
        (D.reflect e • (L.scale * Complex.I)) * (δ : ℂ) := by
    calc
      D.reflect e • ((L.scale * Complex.I) * (δ : ℂ)) =
          D.reflect e • (δ • (L.scale * Complex.I)) := by
            simp [Complex.real_smul, mul_comm, mul_left_comm]
      _ = δ • (D.reflect e • (L.scale * Complex.I)) :=
        smul_comm (D.reflect e) δ (L.scale * Complex.I)
      _ = (D.reflect e • (L.scale * Complex.I)) * (δ : ℂ) := by
        simp [Complex.real_smul, mul_comm]
  have hscaled0 :
      D.reflect e • ((L.scale * Complex.I) * (δ : ℂ)) =
        (-(L.scale * Complex.I)) * (δ : ℂ) := by
    simpa [mul_assoc, mul_left_comm, mul_comm] using hscaled
  have hscaled' : (D.reflect e • (L.scale * Complex.I)) * (δ : ℂ) =
      (-(L.scale * Complex.I)) * (δ : ℂ) := by
    rw [← hcomm]
    exact hscaled0
  exact mul_right_cancel₀ hδc hscaled'

/-- **Advance 8.** The two bounded-window eigendirections determine the action on the entire
developed plane: after multiplication by the local scale, the selected reflection is complex
conjugation globally.  This is the repaired version of Section 176's main linear identity. -/
theorem reflect_scale_mul_eq_scale_mul_star
    {e : E} {W : HalfPlaneWindow}
    (L : WindowFlatLocalEdgeParam (H := H) D V W (1 : G) e)
    (z0 : W.Point)
    (hboundary : ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ).im = 0)
    (z : ℂ) :
    D.reflect e • (L.scale * z) = L.scale * star z := by
  have h1 := reflect_scale (H := H) D V L z0 hboundary
  have hi := reflect_scale_mul_I (H := H) D V L z0 hboundary
  have hz : L.scale * z =
      z.re • L.scale + z.im • (L.scale * Complex.I) := by
    apply Complex.ext <;> simp [Complex.mul_re, Complex.mul_im] <;> ring
  have hzstar : L.scale * star z =
      z.re • L.scale - z.im • (L.scale * Complex.I) := by
    apply Complex.ext <;> simp [Complex.mul_re, Complex.mul_im] <;> ring
  rw [hz, smul_add]
  rw [smul_comm (D.reflect e) z.re L.scale]
  rw [smul_comm (D.reflect e) z.im (L.scale * Complex.I)]
  rw [h1, hi]
  rw [hzstar]
  simp [sub_eq_add_neg]

/-- **Advance 9.** In the globally reframed coordinate `z ↦ scale⁻¹ z`, the repaired bounded
reflection law is literal conjugation on all of `ℂ`.  This is the exact interface needed by the old
finite star-difference argument, now obtained from a genuine compact-polygon patch. -/
theorem inv_scale_reflect_eq_star_inv_scale
    {e : E} {W : HalfPlaneWindow}
    (L : WindowFlatLocalEdgeParam (H := H) D V W (1 : G) e)
    (z0 : W.Point)
    (hboundary : ((z0.1 : EdgeInteriorLocalSeam.UpperHalfPlane) : ℂ).im = 0)
    (w : ℂ) :
    L.scale⁻¹ * (D.reflect e • w) = star (L.scale⁻¹ * w) := by
  have hb : L.scale ≠ 0 := L.scale_ne_zero
  let z : ℂ := L.scale⁻¹ * w
  have hw : L.scale * z = w := by
    dsimp [z]
    field_simp [hb]
  have h := reflect_scale_mul_eq_scale_mul_star
    (H := H) D V L z0 hboundary z
  rw [hw] at h
  have h' := congrArg (fun q : ℂ => L.scale⁻¹ * q) h
  simpa [z, hb, mul_assoc] using h'

/-- **Advance 10.** Every actual unique edge point in the identity copy supplies a nonzero global
normalizing scale with the repaired conjugation law.  The required bounded patch and boundary
parameter are obtained from `BoundedFlatEdgeCover`; hence the final edge normalization no longer
requires an externally chosen historical whole-half-plane chart. -/
theorem exists_edge_normalizing_scale_of_uniqueEdge
    {J : Type uJ}
    (CE : BoundedFlatEdgeCover (G := G) (H := H) D V J)
    (e : E) (p : P) (hp : UniqueEdgeAt (H := H) D e p) :
    ∃ b : ℂ, b ≠ 0 ∧
      ∀ w : ℂ, b⁻¹ * (D.reflect e • w) = star (b⁻¹ * w) := by
  rcases CE.covers_uniqueEdge (1 : G) e p hp with
    ⟨j, hjcopy, hjedge, z0, hz0⟩
  have transport : ∀ (g : G) (f : E)
      (L : WindowFlatLocalEdgeParam (H := H) D V (CE.window j) g f),
      g = 1 → f = e → L.toP z0 = p →
      ∃ b : ℂ, b ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ w : ℂ,
        b⁻¹ * (D.reflect e • w) = star (b⁻¹ * w) := by
    intro g f L hg hf hz
    subst g
    subst f
    have hpz : D.onEdge e (L.toP z0) := by rw [hz]; exact hp.1
    have hboundary := (L.edge_iff_boundary z0).1 hpz
    exact ⟨L.scale, L.scale_ne_zero,
      inv_scale_reflect_eq_star_inv_scale (H := H) D V L z0 hboundary⟩
  exact transport (CE.copy j) (CE.edge j) (CE.patch j) hjcopy hjedge hz0

end BoundedEdgeReflectionScaleIntertwining


/-! ## 304. Updated bounded dynamical boundary after recovering the global reflection derivative

The whole-half-plane dependence of historical Section 176 has now been removed.  A genuine bounded
edge window containing one actual edge point supplies two independent infinitesimal directions by
relative openness in the closed upper half-plane.  Subtracting the two bounded flat formulas shows
that the selected edge reflection fixes `scale` and negates `scale * I`; real-linearity therefore
forces the same global conjugation law as before.  Moreover `BoundedFlatEdgeCover` automatically
supplies such a normalizing scale from any concrete unique edge point in the identity copy.

Consequently the remaining migration no longer needs any new Euclidean reflection calculation.
The next step is purely atlas-theoretic: replace Section 182's historical edge-source finite
star-difference lemmas by their already available bounded side-representation analogues, combine
them with the global law above, and run `FiniteStarDifferenceCompatibility` over the repaired
`BoundedIndex` cover.  That will yield `IsLocallyStarAffine` for the repaired full regular reflection,
after which Sections 184--187 can be reused on the bounded quotient.
-/

/-! ## 305. Bounded finite star-difference migration and repaired full star-affinity

Section 304 recovered the global conjugation derivative from a genuine bounded edge window.  We
now migrate the historical Sections 179, 182, and 183 to the repaired bounded atlas.  The proof is
organized around an arbitrary nonzero normalizing factor `b` satisfying the global reflection law;
Section 304 supplies such a factor from any actual unique edge point.  This keeps the atlas argument
independent of which bounded edge patch was used to detect the reflection derivative.
-/

namespace BoundedConstructedPolygonFullStarAffine

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open FullCopyUnfolding
open FullInteriorFlatCharts
open FlatEdgeChartPotentials
open FlatEdgeCanonicalSideRepresentation
