/-! ## 308. Updated boundary after repaired quotient descent and fixed-mirror construction

The bounded repair has now crossed the full/reduced quotient boundary.  After the single edge scale
normalization, redundancy remains locally translational; the full anti-affine reflection therefore
descends through the effective finite quotient, and local star-affinity survives the canonical
homeomorphism to the actual reduced regular locus.  The resulting normalized reduced surface uses
the same intrinsic regular set as the repaired unnormalized surface.

Moreover no historical seam centre is needed.  Any `UniqueEdgeAt` point of the selected polygon
edge gives a regular full seam class, hence a canonical reduced regular point fixed by the actual
`edgeSigma`.  The restricted reflection is continuous, involutive, locally star-affine, and therefore
nonidentity.  Thus every geometric/topological hypothesis of the fixed-mirror nonminimality bridge is
now present on the compact-polygon-compatible repaired surface.  The next step is genuinely
dynamical: identify its horizontal maximal-leaf direction with the concrete edge-direction flow and
supply/prove the lattice-surface implication from nonminimality to complete periodicity.
-/

/-! ## 309. Repaired fixed mirror to genuine directional nonminimality

Section 308 completed the compact-polygon-compatible reflection geometry on the actual reduced
regular locus.  We now reconnect that repaired mirror to the already-closed abstract maximal-leaf
machinery of Sections 93--100.  No endpoint classification is introduced: the output is exactly a
non-dense maximal regular horizontal leaf, equivalently failure of horizontal minimality.  The last
step to complete periodicity is therefore isolated once again as the genuine leafwise Veech theorem.
-/

