/-! ## 395. Active-edge oriented source sectors and the two genuine polygon seams

Section 394 constructed positive-radius points in the genuine source polygon, but an audit of the
sector automaton exposes one more orientation issue which must be resolved before applying
`SideRel`: the active edge of a `SectorState` is not always `nextEdge`.  The successor replaces it by
`otherEdge`, so along a sector cycle the active side alternates between the two incident sides.

Accordingly, the abstract angular coordinate used by the cyclic sector model must be converted to a
source-polygon angular coordinate depending on the active side.  If the active side is `nextEdge`,
we use `theta`; if it is `prevEdge`, we use `alpha - theta`.  With this convention the right boundary
of every abstract sector is always the active edge and the left boundary is always `otherEdge`.

Before introducing that conversion we prove, directly from the `arg` definition of the oriented
interior angle, that the corrected right boundary ray is exactly the normalized outgoing edge ray.
This closes the geometric seam identification at both sides of the genuine polygon wedge.
-/

namespace CorrectedActiveSectorOrientation

open FullCopyUnfolding
open ConcreteFiniteEuclideanPolygonSource
open GenuinePolygonBoundaryExit
open GenuinePolygonVertexIncidence
open RationalReducedVertexConeArithmetic
open ReducedVertexSectorAutomaton
