/-! ## 405. Converse-kernel bookkeeping after full interior covariance

Section 404 removed the last angular ambiguity created by redundancy: at the final kernel scale the
abstract active angle is literally invariant under `sectorAct`.  We now push that theorem back into
the converse-kernel argument.  The first result below keeps the *full-unfolding* equality carried by
a reduced equality instead of immediately forgetting it to a source-point equality.  The subsequent
lemmas isolate the only remaining source issue: a strict wedge-interior point is not on either of its
two incident sides, and a positive-radius kernel point is never a listed vertex.  Consequently any
still-unaccounted-for side through such a point would have to be a nonincident ("foreign") polygon
edge.  This identifies the exact final source-local separation statement needed before the abstract
sector kernel can be identified with the actual reduced kernel.
