Progress checkpoint after Section 405:

* equality in `Reduced` can now be lifted without discarding the corresponding equality in `Full`;
* every positive kernel-scale sector point is proved to be different from every listed polygon vertex;
* hence such a point lies on at most one listed side, and any side through it is automatically unique;
* a strict active angle excludes both incident sides separately;
* therefore any still-possible side through a strict local sector interior would have to be a
  nonincident (foreign) polygon side;
* the exact remaining source-local theorem has been isolated as `NoForeignEdgeAtKernel`.

For a genuine finite embedded polygon this last statement should be derived, not assumed: each
nonincident listed side is a compact closed segment not containing the chosen vertex, so its distance
from that vertex is positive; a finite minimum over the nonincident sides gives a radius below which
none can occur.  Once that radius is intersected into `kernelRadius`, the theorem
`noEdge_of_strict_kernel_point` feeds directly into `fullMk_eq_fullMk_of_noEdge`, finishing the strict
interior part of the actual converse kernel.  Boundary angles `0` and `alpha` are already covered by
the Section-395/399 seam theorems.
-/

end McMullen313Strict

