/-! ## 406. Foreign-edge separation from the finite embedded polygon source

Section 405 isolated one last source-local obstruction to the strict-interior converse kernel: a
sufficiently small strict wedge point must not meet a nonincident polygon side.  For the genuine
finite Euclidean source this is not an extra hypothesis.  A nonincident listed side is a compact
closed segment missing the chosen vertex, hence the distance from the vertex to that segment has a
strictly positive lower bound.  Finiteness of the side set supplies one common positive clearance.
We intersect this clearance with the previous kernel radius and thereby remove
`NoForeignEdgeAtKernel` from the proof path.
-/

